window.XTY_ARTICLE_TRANSLATIONS = {
  "Carbon equivalent compresses composition into a useful hardenability indicator. It does not know the plate thickness, hydrogen level, restraint, heat input or actual thermal cycle of the joint.": "碳当量把化学成分综合为一个有用的淬硬性指标，但它并不知道钢板厚度、氢含量、拘束度、热输入或接头的实际热循环。",
  "Three equations, three calibration histories": "三个公式，三种不同的校准背景",
  "All elements are mass percentages. The equations are empirical: each was fitted to a particular body of steels and welding experience. CEV is widely reported on European inspection certificates and remains a useful first screen for ferritic structural steels. CET is used in European preheat methods for many modern low-carbon steels. Pcm gives carbon and boron greater influence and is often informative for low-carbon thermo-mechanically processed steels. Similar numerical values do not make the equations interchangeable.": "所有元素均以质量百分数计。这些公式都是经验公式，各自基于特定钢种和焊接经验拟合而成。CEV 广泛列于欧洲材料检验证书中，仍是铁素体结构钢的有效初步筛查指标。CET 用于许多现代低碳钢的欧洲预热计算方法。Pcm 对碳和硼赋予更高权重，常用于评估低碳热机械轧制钢。数值相近并不意味着这些公式可以互换。",
  "What a carbon-equivalent value can tell you": "碳当量能够说明什么",
  "A higher value generally indicates a greater tendency for the HAZ to transform into hard microstructures under a sufficiently rapid cooling cycle. That helps compare heats of broadly similar steel and supports a hydrogen-cracking assessment. It is also useful when reviewing whether the production material remains within the composition envelope assumed by a qualified procedure.": "数值越高，通常表示在足够快的冷却条件下，热影响区形成硬化组织的倾向越大。这有助于比较大体相似钢种的不同炉次，并支持氢致裂纹评估；还可用于核查生产材料是否仍处于已评定工艺所假定的成分范围内。",
  "What it cannot tell you": "它不能说明什么",
  "Hydrogen:": "氢：",
  "consumable classification, drying, exposure, surface moisture and process all affect diffusible hydrogen.": "焊材等级、烘干、暴露时间、表面水分和焊接方法都会影响扩散氢。",
  "Cooling rate:": "冷却速度：",
  "thickness, joint geometry, heat input, preheat and interpass temperature change the thermal cycle.": "板厚、接头几何、热输入、预热和层间温度都会改变热循环。",
  "Restraint and stress:": "拘束与应力：",
  "a short repair in a rigid node is not equivalent to a free plate coupon.": "刚性节点中的短修补焊与可自由变形的平板试件并不等效。",
  "Product route:": "产品制造路线：",
  "Q&T, TMCP and normalized steels can respond differently at the same nominal strength.": "即使名义强度相同，调质钢、TMCP 钢和正火钢的响应也可能不同。",
  "Required properties:": "所需性能：",
  "avoiding cold cracking does not prove HAZ toughness, strength or fatigue performance.": "避免冷裂纹并不能证明热影响区的韧性、强度或疲劳性能合格。",
  "Why “CEV below 0.40 means no preheat” fails": "为什么“CEV 低于 0.40 就无需预热”并不成立",
  "A fixed cut-off ignores every variable above. A thin, low-restraint joint made with controlled low-hydrogen consumables may need no intentional preheat; a highly restrained thick joint from the same heat may require it. Tack welds, attachments and repairs can cool faster or carry more restraint than the main production weld. Ambient temperature and condensation can also change the decision.": "固定阈值忽略了上述所有变量。采用受控低氢焊材的薄板低拘束接头可能无需专门预热，而同一炉次材料的厚板高拘束接头则可能需要预热。定位焊、附件焊和修补焊可能比主体焊缝冷却更快或拘束更大；环境温度和结露也会改变判断。",
  "A defensible EN-based workflow": "一套可追溯的欧标评估流程",
  "Identify the exact product, delivery condition, thickness and ladle analysis from the material certificate.": "从材料证书确认具体产品、交货状态、厚度和熔炼分析。",
  "Use the carbon-equivalent equation required by the governing method; do not select the equation that gives the lowest result.": "使用适用方法规定的碳当量公式，不要挑选结果最低的公式。",
  "Estimate the hydrogen level from the qualified consumable and its handling route.": "根据已评定焊材及其储存、烘干和使用流程估算氢含量。",
  "Define combined thickness, joint geometry, heat input, restraint and initial temperature.": "明确组合厚度、接头几何、热输入、拘束度和初始温度。",
  "Apply the project-adopted method, commonly the framework referenced through EN 1011-2, then check manufacturer limits.": "采用项目规定的方法，通常是 EN 1011-2 所引用的框架，并核对制造商限制。",
  "Verify the result against the WPS/WPQR range and production monitoring capability.": "将结果与 WPS/WPQR 的适用范围及生产监控能力进行核对。",
  "Carbon equivalent is an input to a preheat assessment—not a preheat temperature and not a weldability certificate.": "碳当量只是预热评估的一个输入，不是预热温度，也不是可焊性合格证。",
  "Use the edition and method invoked by the project specification. This article is not a substitute for a qualified WPS.": "应使用项目规范指定的标准版本和方法。本文不能替代经评定的 WPS。",

  "Arc energy describes what the process supplies. t8/5 describes one part of what the steel experiences: the time taken to cool from 800°C to 500°C.": "电弧能量描述焊接过程提供了多少能量；t8/5 描述钢材经历的一个关键阶段，即从 800°C 冷却到 500°C 所需的时间。",
  "Why the 800–500°C interval matters": "为什么 800–500°C 区间很重要",
  "For many ferritic steels, important austenite decomposition reactions occur in this interval. A short t8/5 generally promotes harder transformation products; a long t8/5 favours softer products and greater grain-growth exposure. Continuous-cooling-transformation data can therefore connect an estimated cooling time with likely HAZ microstructure and hardness—but only for the actual steel chemistry and austenitising history.": "对于许多铁素体钢，重要的奥氏体分解反应发生在这一温度区间。较短的 t8/5 通常促进较硬的转变产物；较长的 t8/5 则有利于较软组织形成，并增加晶粒长大暴露。连续冷却转变数据可以把估算冷却时间与可能的热影响区组织和硬度联系起来，但仅适用于实际钢材成分和奥氏体化历程。",
  "Heat input does not uniquely define t8/5": "热输入不能唯一决定 t8/5",
  "The same calculated heat input can produce different cooling times. A thin sheet loses heat mainly in two dimensions; a thick plate can conduct heat in three dimensions. A fillet weld, butt weld and root pass have different heat sinks. Preheat raises the starting temperature, interpass temperature changes later passes, and bead sequence reheats earlier HAZ regions.": "相同的计算热输入可能产生不同的冷却时间。薄板主要以二维方式散热，厚板则可能发生三维导热；角焊缝、对接焊缝和根焊道的散热条件也不同。预热提高起始温度，层间温度影响后续焊道，焊道顺序还会再次加热先前形成的热影响区。",
  "Variable": "变量",
  "Typical influence on cooling": "对冷却的典型影响",
  "Higher arc energy / heat input": "较高的电弧能量／热输入",
  "Usually increases t8/5, but process efficiency and geometry matter": "通常会延长 t8/5，但仍受工艺效率和几何条件影响",
  "Higher preheat or interpass temperature": "较高的预热或道间温度",
  "Reduces the temperature gradient and usually slows cooling": "减小温度梯度，通常使冷却变慢",
  "Greater effective thickness / heat sink": "更大的有效厚度／散热能力",
  "Can shorten t8/5 for the same weld parameters": "在相同焊接参数下可能缩短 t8/5",
  "Short bead, run-off or start/stop": "短焊道、引出端或起停位置",
  "Creates transient conditions not represented by steady-state calculations": "产生稳态计算无法反映的瞬态条件",
  "Multipass reheating": "多道焊再热",
  "Produces intercritically and subcritically reheated HAZ regions": "形成临界间和亚临界再热热影响区",
  "The HAZ is not one homogeneous band": "热影响区并不是均一的一条带",
  "Coarse-grained HAZ:": "粗晶热影响区：",
  "reaches well above the upper critical temperature; prior-austenite grain growth can reduce toughness.": "峰值温度明显高于上临界温度；原奥氏体晶粒长大可能降低韧性。",
  "Fine-grained HAZ:": "细晶热影响区：",
  "fully austenitised at a lower peak temperature and may show grain refinement.": "在较低峰值温度下完全奥氏体化，可能出现晶粒细化。",
  "Intercritical HAZ:": "临界间热影响区：",
  "only partly austenitised; in Q&T and some TMCP steels it can contain locally softened or brittle constituents.": "仅部分奥氏体化；在调质钢和某些 TMCP 钢中可能出现局部软化或脆性组分。",
  "Subcritical HAZ:": "亚临界热影响区：",
  "does not re-austenitise, but tempering can reduce hardness and strength in quenched-and-tempered steel.": "不发生再奥氏体化，但回火可能降低调质钢的硬度和强度。",
  "Why both a lower and an upper heat-input bound may be needed": "为什么热输入可能同时需要上下限",
  "Too little thermal input can cause rapid cooling, high hardness and hydrogen-cracking sensitivity. Too much can enlarge the coarse-grained HAZ, reduce toughness or create an excessively wide softened zone. For S690 and S960 products, the acceptable window depends on the exact product and thickness; the manufacturer’s welding guide and the qualified procedure matter more than a generic steel-grade rule.": "热输入过低可能导致快速冷却、高硬度和较高的氢致裂纹敏感性；热输入过高则可能扩大粗晶热影响区、降低韧性，或形成过宽的软化区。对于 S690 和 S960 产品，可接受窗口取决于具体产品和厚度；制造商焊接指南和经评定工艺比笼统的钢级规则更重要。",
  "Using t8/5 in procedure development": "在工艺开发中使用 t8/5",
  "Obtain the product-specific recommended t8/5 or heat-input range where available.": "如有资料，取得针对具体产品的建议 t8/5 或热输入范围。",
  "Estimate cooling time for the real joint geometry, effective thickness and preheat.": "针对实际接头几何、有效厚度和预热条件估算冷却时间。",
  "Qualify the proposed window using representative welding parameters and bead placement.": "使用具有代表性的焊接参数和焊道布置评定拟定窗口。",
  "Measure hardness and required strength/toughness at the relevant HAZ locations.": "在相关热影响区位置测量硬度及所需强度／韧性。",
  "Translate the qualified result into controllable WPS limits: voltage, current, travel speed, bead size, preheat and maximum interpass temperature.": "把评定结果转化为可控制的 WPS 限值：电压、电流、焊接速度、焊道尺寸、预热和最高层间温度。",
  "Check starts, stops, tack welds and repair welds separately when their thermal cycles are more severe.": "当起弧、收弧、定位焊和修补焊的热循环更严苛时，应分别进行核查。",
  "Heat input is not a material property. A qualified thermal window belongs to a defined steel product, thickness, joint and welding sequence.": "热输入不是材料性能。经评定的热循环窗口只属于明确的钢材产品、厚度、接头和焊接顺序。",
  "Calculated t8/5 values should be checked against the project method and, where critical, validated by measurement or representative procedure testing.": "计算得到的 t8/5 应与项目采用的方法核对；在关键情况下，还应通过测量或有代表性的工艺试验验证。",

  "Hydrogen-assisted cold cracking is not caused by hydrogen alone. It appears when diffusible hydrogen, a susceptible microstructure, tensile stress and a suitable temperature-time history overlap.": "氢致冷裂纹并非由氢单独造成。只有当扩散氢、敏感组织、拉应力以及合适的温度—时间历程同时存在时，裂纹才会出现。",
  "1. A source of diffusible hydrogen": "1. 扩散氢来源",
  "Moisture in electrode coverings or flux, contaminated wire, damp joint surfaces, paint, oil and humid shielding systems can introduce hydrogen into the weld pool. The relevant quantity is diffusible—not total—hydrogen. A low-hydrogen consumable classification is only useful when storage, baking, exposure limits and handling preserve it through production.": "焊条药皮或焊剂中的水分、受污染的焊丝、潮湿接头表面、油漆、油污以及含湿保护气系统，都可能把氢带入熔池。真正相关的是扩散氢，而不是总氢。只有在储存、烘干、暴露时限和使用过程都得到控制时，低氢焊材等级才有意义。",
  "2. A susceptible local microstructure": "2. 敏感的局部组织",
  "Rapid cooling can form hard martensitic or bainitic regions in the HAZ. Susceptibility depends on composition, prior microstructure and local thermal cycle, which is why carbon equivalent and t8/5 are supporting inputs. Cracks can also occur in weld metal, particularly in high-strength deposits; an acceptable HAZ hardness alone does not close the assessment.": "快速冷却可能在热影响区形成硬的马氏体或贝氏体区域。敏感性取决于化学成分、原始组织和局部热循环，因此碳当量和 t8/5 只是辅助输入。裂纹也可能出现在焊缝金属中，尤其是高强度熔敷金属；仅有合格的热影响区硬度不足以完成评估。",
  "3. Tensile stress and restraint": "3. 拉应力与拘束",
  "Weld shrinkage generates residual tensile stress even without external load. Thick T-joints, attachments, closed frames, repairs and poorly sequenced welds increase restraint. Root notches, lack of fusion and sharp weld toes concentrate stress. A procedure qualified on a freely moving plate may therefore be less severe than the production joint.": "即使没有外载，焊接收缩也会产生残余拉应力。厚板 T 形接头、附件、封闭框架、修补焊以及不合理的焊接顺序都会增加拘束。根部缺口、未熔合和尖锐焊趾会造成应力集中。因此，在可自由变形钢板上评定的工艺，其严苛程度可能低于实际生产接头。",
  "4. Temperature and time": "4. 温度与时间",
  "Cracking is often delayed because hydrogen needs time to diffuse toward highly stressed microstructural traps. The critical interval is commonly after the weld has cooled, not while the arc is present. Immediate NDT can therefore miss cracks that develop later. Required inspection delay must come from the governing code and project risk assessment.": "裂纹常具有延迟性，因为氢需要时间向高应力的组织陷阱扩散。关键时段通常是在焊缝冷却以后，而不是电弧燃烧期间。因此，立即进行无损检测可能漏掉随后形成的裂纹。所需检测延迟时间必须依据适用规范和项目风险评估确定。",
  "Prevention is a system": "预防必须依靠系统控制",
  "Control": "控制措施",
  "What it changes": "它改变什么",
  "What it does not guarantee": "它不能保证什么",
  "Low-hydrogen consumables and dry surfaces": "低氢焊材和干燥表面",
  "Reduces available hydrogen": "减少可用氢",
  "Does not remove restraint or hard microstructure": "不能消除拘束或硬化组织",
  "Preheat": "预热",
  "Slows cooling and promotes hydrogen diffusion": "减缓冷却并促进氢扩散",
  "Does not justify unlimited heat input or interpass temperature": "不能成为无限提高热输入或层间温度的理由",
  "Controlled heat input and bead size": "控制热输入和焊道尺寸",
  "Controls the local thermal cycle": "控制局部热循环",
  "Does not compensate for wet consumables": "不能弥补焊材受潮",
  "Joint redesign and sequence": "优化接头设计和焊接顺序",
  "Reduces restraint and stress concentration": "降低拘束和应力集中",
  "Does not remove material susceptibility": "不能消除材料敏感性",
  "Delayed NDT": "延迟无损检测",
  "Improves probability of detecting delayed cracks": "提高发现延迟裂纹的概率",
  "Detects rather than prevents cracking": "只能检测裂纹，不能预防裂纹",
  "Where postheat fits": "后热的作用位置",
  "A controlled dehydrogenation treatment immediately after welding can extend the time at elevated temperature and assist hydrogen diffusion. It is not the same as stress-relief PWHT. Temperature, duration, heating rate and transfer time must be qualified for the actual steel. Applying a generic 200–350°C treatment to quenched-and-tempered high-strength steel can temper the HAZ or parent material and reduce properties.": "焊后立即进行受控去氢处理，可以延长高温停留时间并促进氢扩散。它不同于消除应力热处理。温度、保温时间、升温速率和转移时间必须针对实际钢材进行评定。对调质高强钢套用通用的 200–350°C 处理，可能使热影响区或母材发生回火并降低性能。",
  "Diagnosing a suspected crack": "诊断疑似裂纹",
  "Map the crack position relative to weld metal, fusion boundary and HAZ.": "标明裂纹相对于焊缝金属、熔合线和热影响区的位置。",
  "Review time of discovery, consumable batches, exposure logs and environmental conditions.": "复核发现时间、焊材批次、暴露记录和环境条件。",
  "Reconstruct actual heat input, preheat, interpass temperature and sequence.": "重建实际热输入、预热、层间温度和焊接顺序。",
  "Assess local hardness, microstructure, fracture morphology and joint restraint together.": "综合评估局部硬度、显微组织、断口形貌和接头拘束。",
  "Do not treat EDX detection of an element as proof of the cracking mechanism by itself.": "不要把 EDX 检出的某种元素单独作为裂纹机理的证明。",
  "Before repair, remove the cause and qualify the excavation, preheat and repair sequence.": "修补前应先消除根因，并评定清除范围、预热和修补顺序。",
  "“Low hydrogen” is a production system, not a label printed on a box of electrodes.": "“低氢”是一套生产控制体系，而不只是焊条包装上的标签。",

  "S960 is a strength class, not a complete welding specification. The exact product, delivery condition, thickness, joint and required properties define the usable thermal window.": "S960 是一个强度等级，不是一份完整的焊接规范。具体产品、交货状态、厚度、接头形式和所需性能共同决定可用的热循环窗口。",
  "Where the plate strength comes from": "钢板强度从何而来",
  "Many S960 plate products achieve their properties through quenching and tempering; other high-strength products may use different thermomechanical routes. Their microstructures are engineered by chemistry and heat treatment. Welding locally reheats that structure above, within or below the austenitising range, creating several HAZ sub-zones with different properties.": "许多 S960 钢板通过淬火和回火获得其性能，其他高强钢产品也可能采用不同的热机械路线。其显微组织由化学成分和热处理共同设计。焊接会使该组织在局部重新加热到奥氏体化区间以上、以内或以下，从而形成性能不同的多个热影响区子区域。",
  "Too fast: hardness and hydrogen-cracking risk": "冷却过快：硬度与氢致裂纹风险",
  "Low heat input, a large heat sink and low initial temperature can shorten t8/5. The resulting hard microstructure can be sensitive to hydrogen-assisted cracking when diffusible hydrogen and restraint are present. The lower bound is therefore connected to consumable hydrogen, preheat, effective thickness, carbon equivalent and joint restraint—not heat input alone.": "低热输入、较强散热条件和较低初始温度会缩短 t8/5。当扩散氢和拘束同时存在时，由此形成的硬化组织可能对氢致裂纹敏感。因此，下限与焊材氢含量、预热、有效厚度、碳当量和接头拘束有关，而不只取决于热输入。",
  "Too slow: coarse grains and softening": "冷却过慢：晶粒粗化与软化",
  "High heat input or excessive interpass temperature can lengthen cooling time, widen the HAZ and promote grain growth or tempering. In Q&T steel, subcritical and intercritical regions can soften relative to the delivered plate. Whether that soft zone reduces joint resistance depends on its width, location, strength mismatch and the structural stress state.": "高热输入或过高层间温度会延长冷却时间、加宽热影响区，并促进晶粒长大或回火。在调质钢中，亚临界和临界间区域可能相对交货态钢板发生软化。该软化区是否降低接头承载力，取决于其宽度、位置、强度错配和结构应力状态。",
  "The window belongs to a defined case": "窗口只适用于明确的工况",
  "Input": "输入因素",
  "Why it changes the result": "为什么会改变结果",
  "Product and thickness": "产品与厚度",
  "Chemistry, delivered properties and heat sink vary": "化学成分、交货性能和散热条件不同",
  "Joint geometry": "接头几何",
  "Butt, fillet, root and repair welds dissipate heat differently": "对接焊、角焊、根焊和修补焊的散热方式不同",
  "Process and bead size": "工艺与焊道尺寸",
  "Efficiency, deposition and reheating pattern change": "效率、熔敷量和再热模式发生变化",
  "Preheat/interpass": "预热／层间温度",
  "Controls cooling and accumulated thermal exposure": "控制冷却和累积热暴露",
  "Consumable": "焊材",
  "Strength, toughness and hydrogen level affect cracking and deformation": "强度、韧性和氢含量影响开裂与变形",
  "Required property": "所需性能",
  "Static strength, toughness, fatigue and fracture may govern differently": "静力强度、韧性、疲劳和断裂可能分别控制设计",
  "From manufacturer guidance to a WPS": "从制造商指南到 WPS",
  "Start with the exact plate manufacturer’s welding recommendations and inspection certificate.": "首先查阅具体钢板制造商的焊接建议和材料检验证书。",
  "Select compatible low-hydrogen consumables with adequate toughness at the design temperature.": "选择与母材相容、在设计温度下具有足够韧性的低氢焊材。",
  "Establish preliminary preheat, interpass and heat-input limits for the real joint and thickness.": "针对实际接头和厚度确定初步预热、层间温度和热输入限值。",
  "Qualify a representative procedure, including the most severe bead location and process sequence.": "评定具有代表性的工艺，包括最严苛的焊道位置和工艺顺序。",
  "Check tensile strength, fracture location, impact properties where required, hardness and HAZ softening.": "检查抗拉强度、断裂位置、必要时的冲击性能、硬度和热影响区软化。",
  "Convert the successful test into ranges that production equipment can monitor.": "把成功的试验结果转化为生产设备可以监控的参数范围。",
  "Control tack, attachment and repair welds; small welds can create severe local cooling conditions.": "控制定位焊、附件焊和修补焊；小焊缝可能形成严苛的局部冷却条件。",
  "What the Hong Kong application demonstrates": "香港应用案例说明了什么",
  "Public information on the Fanling North footbridge work describes S960 box girders fabricated using welding technology developed through testing and numerical simulation for different thicknesses and joint designs. The engineering lesson is not a single transferable heat-input number. It is the method: link product, geometry, thermal cycle and joint performance before production.": "粉岭北行人天桥的公开资料介绍了 S960 箱梁的制造，所用焊接技术通过针对不同厚度和接头设计的试验与数值模拟开发。该案例的工程启示不是一个可以直接移用的热输入数值，而是一套方法：生产前把产品、几何、热循环和接头性能联系起来。",
  "The plate certificate proves delivered material properties. Only a representative qualified procedure can demonstrate the welded joint.": "钢板证书证明的是交货态材料性能；只有具有代表性的经评定工艺，才能证明焊接接头的性能。",

  "Z-Quality Steel and Lamellar Tearing: What Z15, Z25 and Z35 Really Mean": "Z 向性能钢与层状撕裂：Z15、Z25 和 Z35 的真正含义",
  "Z-quality describes verified ductility through the plate thickness. Lamellar-tearing resistance still depends on joint detail, weld shrinkage, restraint, cleanliness and the actual plate location.": "Z 向性能表示经验证的钢板厚度方向延性。抗层状撕裂能力仍取决于接头细节、焊接收缩、拘束、洁净度以及钢板的实际取样位置。",
  "Why rolled plate is directionally different": "为什么轧制钢板具有方向差异",
  "Rolling elongates non-metallic inclusions parallel to the plate surface. Strength and ductility are normally best in the rolling plane and weaker through the thickness. When weld contraction pulls across the plate thickness, strain can concentrate between inclusion arrays. The resulting stepped crack is usually located in the parent plate, roughly parallel to its surface.": "轧制会使非金属夹杂沿平行于钢板表面的方向延伸。强度和延性通常在轧制平面内最好，而厚度方向较弱。当焊接收缩沿厚度方向拉伸钢板时，应变会集中在夹杂物带之间，由此产生的阶梯状裂纹通常位于母材内，并大致平行于钢板表面。",
  "What EN 10164 classifies": "EN 10164 对什么进行分级",
  "EN 10164 specifies products with improved deformation properties perpendicular to the surface. The class number refers to the minimum average reduction of area measured in a through-thickness tensile test. It is not a sulfur grade and not a direct crack-resistance percentage.": "EN 10164 规定了垂直于产品表面方向具有改进变形性能的钢材。等级数字表示厚度方向拉伸试验测得的最小平均断面收缩率；它不是硫含量等级，也不是直接的抗裂百分比。",
  "Class": "等级",
  "Minimum average reduction of area": "最小平均断面收缩率",
  "Minimum individual value": "单个试样最小值",
  "Therefore, Z35 does not require every specimen to reach 35%. The average must reach 35%, while no individual result may fall below 25%. Sulfur control and calcium treatment can improve performance, but EN 10164 classes are defined by test results rather than a universal sulfur limit.": "因此，Z35 并不要求每个试样都达到 35%。平均值必须达到 35%，同时任何单个结果不得低于 25%。控制硫含量和进行钙处理可以改善性能，但 EN 10164 的等级由试验结果定义，而不是由统一的硫含量限值定义。",
  "Details that create risk": "容易产生风险的构造细节",
  "Large single-sided fillet or partial-penetration welds on the face of a thick plate.": "厚板表面的大尺寸单面角焊缝或部分熔透焊缝。",
  "T-, corner- and cruciform joints that transmit shrinkage through the thickness.": "使收缩应变沿厚度方向传递的 T 形、角接和十字接头。",
  "Highly restrained nodes where the plate cannot deform in-plane.": "钢板无法在平面内变形的高拘束节点。",
  "Large weld volume, poor fit-up or unnecessary overwelding.": "焊缝体积过大、装配不良或不必要的超量焊接。",
  "Welds close to plate edges or areas with inclusion segregation.": "靠近钢板边缘或夹杂偏析区域的焊缝。",
  "Design before specification": "先优化设计，再规定材料",
  "The most reliable control is to redirect shrinkage strain. Use a joint that allows deformation in the rolling plane; reduce weld volume; balance the sequence; use full-penetration details where they improve the stress path; or orient the plate so the critical stress does not act through thickness. A buttering layer can move the shrinkage strain or reduce restraint, but it needs a qualified sequence.": "最可靠的控制方法是改变收缩应变的传递方向。可采用允许钢板在轧制平面内变形的接头、减少焊缝体积、平衡焊接顺序、在有利于应力路径时采用全熔透构造，或调整钢板方向，使关键应力不沿厚度方向作用。隔离层堆焊可转移收缩应变或降低拘束，但必须采用经评定的工艺顺序。",
  "When Z-quality and parent-plate UT help": "何时需要 Z 向性能和母材超声检测",
  "Z-quality is appropriate when design assessment shows meaningful through-thickness strain demand that cannot be removed by detailing. Selection should follow the relevant design method—such as the European framework associated with EN 1993-1-10—or a project risk assessment, not a rule such as “use Z35 above 50 mm.” Ultrasonic testing around critical attachment zones can identify laminations, but a clear UT result does not measure ductility and is not a substitute for Z-quality when the design requires it.": "当设计评估表明存在不可通过构造消除的显著厚度方向应变需求时，采用 Z 向性能钢是合适的。等级选择应遵循相关设计方法，例如与 EN 1993-1-10 相关的欧洲框架，或项目风险评估，而不是“超过 50 mm 一律使用 Z35”之类的规则。关键附件区域周围的超声检测可以识别分层，但合格的 UT 结果并不能测量延性；当设计要求 Z 向性能时，UT 不能替代它。",
  "A practical review sequence": "实用审查顺序",
  "Mark where weld shrinkage and service load act through the plate thickness.": "标出焊接收缩和使用荷载沿钢板厚度方向作用的位置。",
  "Estimate restraint, effective weld size and consequence of cracking.": "评估拘束度、有效焊缝尺寸和开裂后果。",
  "Redesign the joint where possible.": "在可能的情况下重新优化接头。",
  "Select the required Z-class using the governing design/project method.": "采用适用的设计或项目方法选择所需 Z 等级。",
  "Define any parent-material UT zone and acceptance criteria before fabrication.": "制造前明确母材 UT 区域和验收准则。",
  "Maintain plate identity after cutting so the specified property remains traceable.": "切割后保持钢板身份标识，使规定性能可追溯。",
  "Z35 is evidence of through-thickness ductility. It is not permission to ignore a poor joint detail.": "Z35 是厚度方向延性的证据，不是忽略不良接头细节的许可。",

  "“Use filler stronger than the parent steel” sounds safe, but it can increase restraint, alloy content and hydrogen-cracking sensitivity without improving the governing joint resistance.": "“使用比母材更强的焊材”听起来很安全，但它可能增加拘束、合金含量和氢致裂纹敏感性，却未必提高控制性的接头承载力。",
  "First define what is being matched": "首先明确匹配的是什么",
  "Matching can refer to specified yield strength, tensile strength or actual batch properties. A filler classification may state minimum all-weld-metal properties under a prescribed test condition; it does not guarantee identical properties in every production weld. Dilution, heat input, bead sequence, shielding gas and cooling rate all change the deposit.": "匹配可能指规定屈服强度、抗拉强度或实际批次性能。焊材等级可能规定特定试验条件下全焊缝金属的最低性能，但不能保证每条生产焊缝都具有完全相同的性能。稀释、热输入、焊道顺序、保护气体和冷却速度都会改变熔敷金属。",
  "Three strategies": "三种策略",
  "Strategy": "策略",
  "Possible reason": "可能的原因",
  "Main caution": "主要注意事项",
  "Matching": "等强匹配",
  "Keep nominal weld strength comparable with the governing parent steel": "使焊缝名义强度与控制母材相当",
  "Actual weld and parent strengths may still differ substantially": "实际焊缝与母材强度仍可能相差很大",
  "Overmatching": "超强匹配",
  "Encourage plastic deformation away from the weld in a highly loaded butt joint": "使高受力对接接头的塑性变形远离焊缝",
  "May reduce weld-metal ductility/toughness or increase alloy and hydrogen sensitivity": "可能降低焊缝金属延性／韧性，或增加合金化程度和氢敏感性",
  "Undermatching": "低匹配",
  "Improve weldability and ductility, or suit a joint whose design demand is below parent yield": "改善可焊性和延性，或适用于设计需求低于母材屈服强度的接头",
  "Requires explicit strength and deformation assessment; not suitable by assumption": "需要明确的强度和变形评估，不能凭假设采用",
  "The design check and filler choice are related—but different": "设计验算与焊材选择相关，但并不相同",
  "The structural code defines the resistance of the weld or connected parts. Consumable selection must then deliver the properties assumed by that calculation. For a fillet weld between dissimilar grades, design resistance is commonly governed by the weaker connected material or the weld design rule. That does not automatically mean “always use filler for the lower grade”; toughness, service temperature, dilution, fatigue, coating and procedure qualification remain part of the choice.": "结构规范规定焊缝或连接构件的承载力，焊材选择则必须提供计算所假定的性能。对于不同钢级之间的角焊缝，设计承载力通常由较弱的连接材料或焊缝设计规则控制，但这并不自动意味着“始终按较低钢级选焊材”；韧性、使用温度、稀释、疲劳、涂层和工艺评定仍是选择的一部分。",
  "High-strength steel changes the trade-off": "高强钢改变了权衡关系",
  "As strength increases, achieving a high-strength deposit with adequate toughness and low diffusible hydrogen becomes more demanding. Very strong weld metal can concentrate strain in a softened HAZ. Conversely, a deliberately undermatched deposit may localise deformation in the weld. Either can be acceptable only when the joint geometry and limit state have been assessed.": "随着强度提高，要获得兼具足够韧性和低扩散氢的高强熔敷金属会更加困难。过强的焊缝金属可能使应变集中在软化热影响区；相反，有意采用低匹配熔敷金属也可能使变形集中在焊缝中。只有在对接头几何和极限状态进行评估后，这两种情况才可能被接受。",
  "Dissimilar-strength joints": "异强度接头",
  "Identify which connected component and limit state govern the joint resistance.": "确定哪个连接构件和哪种极限状态控制接头承载力。",
  "Check the actual product standards, thickness-dependent properties and service temperature.": "核对实际产品标准、随厚度变化的性能和使用温度。",
  "Select a compatible consumable classification with suitable strength, impact class and hydrogen designation.": "选择相容且具有合适强度、冲击等级和氢等级的焊材。",
  "Consider dilution from both parent steels and any coating or backing material.": "考虑两侧母材以及任何涂层或衬垫材料造成的稀释。",
  "Qualify the real combination within the applicable material grouping and thickness range.": "在适用材料组别和厚度范围内评定实际组合。",
  "Verify transverse tensile location, weld-metal toughness where required, hardness and any HAZ softening relevant to the design.": "验证横向拉伸断裂位置、必要时的焊缝金属韧性、硬度以及与设计相关的热影响区软化。",
  "A useful review question": "一个有效的审查问题",
  "Instead of asking “Which electrode matches S690?”, ask: “What strength, toughness, hydrogen level and deformation behaviour does this particular joint require, and what qualification evidence proves the proposed consumable delivers them?” That question exposes hidden assumptions about grade, thickness, joint type and code system.": "不要只问“哪种焊条与 S690 匹配？”，而应问：“这个具体接头需要怎样的强度、韧性、氢含量和变形行为？什么评定证据能够证明拟用焊材可以实现这些要求？”这个问题会揭示关于钢级、厚度、接头类型和规范体系的隐藏假设。",
  "The strongest available filler is not automatically the safest or most efficient filler.": "可获得的最高强度焊材，并不自动等于最安全或最高效的焊材。",

  "WPS and PQR: From Procedure Requirements to Qualification Evidence": "WPS 与 PQR：从工艺要求到评定证据",
  "A WPS tells production how to weld. A WPQR or PQR records how a test joint was welded and what that evidence qualified. Confusing instruction with evidence is a common audit failure.": "WPS 告诉生产人员应如何焊接；WPQR 或 PQR 记录试验接头实际如何焊接，以及这些证据评定了什么范围。把指令与证据混为一谈，是审核中常见的问题。",
  "What each document does": "每份文件的作用",
  "Document": "文件",
  "Primary purpose": "主要目的",
  "Typical content": "典型内容",
  "Proposed instructions used to make a qualification weld": "用于制作工艺评定焊缝的拟定指令",
  "Planned joint, materials, process, consumables, positions and parameter ranges": "计划采用的接头、材料、工艺、焊材、位置和参数范围",
  "WPQR / PQR": "WPQR / PQR",
  "Permanent record of the actual qualification variables and test results": "实际评定变量和试验结果的永久记录",
  "Actual material certificates, parameters, NDT, destructive tests and approval range basis": "实际材料证书、参数、无损检测、破坏性试验和认可范围依据",
  "WPS": "WPS",
  "Controlled production instruction within the qualified range": "在评定范围内受控的生产指令",
  "Permitted ranges that a welder, operator and inspector can execute and verify": "焊工、操作员和检验员能够执行并核查的允许范围",
  "Recorded values are not instruction ranges": "记录值不等于工艺指令范围",
  "If the qualification coupon was welded at 245 A, the PQR records 245 A as an actual value. The production WPS may specify an allowable range only when the governing standard and qualification evidence support it. Copying broad machine settings into the PQR weakens the evidence; copying one exact PQR value into the WPS can make production unnecessarily rigid.": "如果评定试件以 245 A 焊接，PQR 应把 245 A 记录为实际值。只有在适用标准和评定证据支持时，生产 WPS 才能规定一个允许范围。把宽泛的设备设定抄入 PQR 会削弱证据；把 PQR 的单一实际值原样抄入 WPS，则可能使生产受到不必要的限制。",
  "The real question is applicability": "真正的问题是适用性",
  "Possessing a signed PQR is not enough. The reviewer must compare its approval range with the production material group, thickness, weld-metal thickness, diameter, joint type, process, position, backing, consumable, heat input, preheat and post-weld treatment. The companion article on essential variables explains this check in detail.": "仅持有一份已签署的 PQR 并不足够。审查人员必须把其认可范围与生产中的材料组别、母材厚度、熔敷金属厚度、直径、接头类型、工艺、位置、衬垫、焊材、热输入、预热和焊后处理逐项比较。关于重要变素的配套文章对这一检查作了详细说明。",
  "ISO and AWS terminology": "ISO 与 AWS 的术语",
  "ISO 15609-1 specifies WPS content and ISO 15614-1 provides a procedure-test route and range of qualification. AWS D1.1 uses its own WPS/PQR terminology and also provides a prequalified route under tightly defined conditions. An AWS prequalified WPS is not an ISO pWPS, and an ISO WPQR does not automatically satisfy AWS.": "ISO 15609-1 规定 WPS 内容，ISO 15614-1 提供工艺试验路线和评定范围。AWS D1.1 使用其自身的 WPS/PQR 术语，并在严格规定的条件下提供免评定路线。AWS 的免评定 WPS 不是 ISO 的 pWPS，ISO WPQR 也不会自动满足 AWS 要求。",
  "What makes a WPS usable on the shop floor": "怎样的 WPS 才能在车间使用",
  "A unique number, revision and approval status linked to the drawing and weld map.": "与图纸和焊缝图关联的唯一编号、版本和批准状态。",
  "Unambiguous material group, thickness and joint detail.": "明确无歧义的材料组别、厚度和接头细节。",
  "Executable ranges for current, voltage, travel speed and heat input.": "可执行的电流、电压、焊接速度和热输入范围。",
  "Consumable classification, diameter, shielding gas and hydrogen handling.": "焊材分类、直径、保护气体和氢控制要求。",
  "Minimum preheat, maximum interpass temperature, measurement location and method.": "最低预热温度、最高层间温度、测量位置和方法。",
  "Pass sequence, bead technique, cleaning, gouging, backing and restart instructions.": "焊道顺序、运条方法、清理、碳弧气刨、衬垫和重新起弧要求。",
  "What makes a PQR credible": "怎样的 PQR 才可信",
  "Material certificates and consumable identification match the coupon.": "材料证书和焊材标识与试件相符。",
  "Actual welding parameters and temperature records are contemporaneous.": "实际焊接参数和温度记录在焊接过程中同步形成。",
  "NDT and specimen locations correspond to the tested joint.": "无损检测和试样位置与受试接头相对应。",
  "Laboratory reports identify method, result, requirement and fracture location.": "实验室报告明确试验方法、结果、要求和断裂位置。",
  "Any deviation or failed specimen has a documented disposition.": "任何偏差或不合格试样都有书面处置记录。",
  "The qualification range is traceable to the correct code edition.": "评定范围可追溯至正确的标准版本。",
  "A WPS without qualification evidence is an instruction without proof. A PQR without an applicability check is proof without a defined use.": "没有评定证据的 WPS 是缺乏证明的指令；未经适用性检查的 PQR 是用途不明的证明。",

  "A procedure qualification does not approve a company to “weld steel.” It supports a defined range of materials, dimensions, processes, consumables and operating conditions.": "工艺评定并不是批准一家公司笼统地“焊接钢材”，而是支持明确范围内的材料、尺寸、工艺、焊材和操作条件。",
  "The document chain": "文件链条",
  "pWPS → qualification weld → examination and tests → WPQR/PQR → production WPS": "pWPS → 评定焊缝 → 检验与试验 → WPQR/PQR → 生产 WPS",
  "The qualification record captures what was actually welded and tested. The production WPS turns the permitted range into instructions. A review therefore starts with the production joint, not with the certificate cover page.": "评定记录反映实际焊接和试验的内容；生产 WPS 则把允许范围转化为操作指令。因此，审查应从生产接头开始，而不是从证书封面开始。",
  "Variables that define the envelope": "定义适用边界的变量",
  "Variable family": "变量类别",
  "Examples to verify": "需要核查的示例",
  "Parent material": "母材",
  "Material group, sub-group, grade, delivery condition and combination": "材料组别、子组、钢级、交货状态和组合",
  "Dimensions": "尺寸",
  "Parent thickness, deposited weld-metal thickness and pipe diameter": "母材厚度、熔敷金属厚度和管径",
  "Process": "焊接方法",
  "ISO 4063 process, degree of mechanisation, process sequence and metal transfer where applicable": "ISO 4063 工艺编号、机械化程度、工艺顺序，以及适用时的熔滴过渡形式",
  "Joint": "接头",
  "Butt/fillet, full/partial penetration, backing, gouging, root technique and position": "对接／角接、全熔透／部分熔透、衬垫、清根、根部技术和焊接位置",
  "Consumables": "焊材",
  "Classification, designation, diameter, flux-wire combination and shielding gas": "分类、牌号、直径、焊剂—焊丝组合和保护气体",
  "Thermal controls": "热控制",
  "Heat-input range, minimum preheat, maximum interpass, PWHT or dehydrogenation treatment": "热输入范围、最低预热、最高层间温度、焊后热处理或去氢处理",
  "Why a thicker test coupon does not cover everything": "为什么更厚的试件并不能覆盖一切",
  "Thickness is only one approval dimension. A qualification made with process 135 does not automatically approve 136; a butt-weld qualification does not necessarily cover every fillet-weld production condition; a change in material group or backing can fall outside the approval. Even where a variable remains inside the formal range, the WPS must still be technically suitable for the joint and service requirement.": "厚度只是认可范围的一个维度。采用 135 工艺完成的评定不会自动认可 136；对接焊评定也不一定覆盖所有角焊缝生产条件；材料组别或衬垫的变化可能超出认可范围。即使某变量仍处于形式上的评定范围内，WPS 也必须在技术上适合实际接头和使用要求。",
  "ISO 15614-1 and AWS D1.1 are different routes": "ISO 15614-1 与 AWS D1.1 是不同的路线",
  "ISO 15614-1 defines qualification by welding procedure test and a range of qualification. ISO 15609-1 defines the content of an arc-welding WPS. AWS D1.1 uses its own essential-variable tables and also permits prequalified WPSs when every stated condition is met. “Prequalified” in AWS is not an ISO qualification route, and an ISO WPQR cannot be assumed to satisfy AWS without a contractual basis.": "ISO 15614-1 规定通过焊接工艺试验进行评定及其评定范围；ISO 15609-1 规定电弧焊 WPS 的内容。AWS D1.1 使用自身的重要变素表，并在满足全部规定条件时允许采用免评定 WPS。AWS 中的“免评定”不是 ISO 的评定路线，没有合同依据时，也不能假定 ISO WPQR 满足 AWS。",
  "How to review coverage efficiently": "如何高效审查覆盖范围",
  "List the production material, thickness, joint, position, process and required properties in one column.": "在第一栏列出生产材料、厚度、接头、位置、工艺和所需性能。",
  "Record the actual qualification-weld variables and test results in a second column.": "在第二栏记录评定焊缝的实际变量和试验结果。",
  "Use the governing standard to derive each permitted range in a third column.": "在第三栏依据适用标准推导每项允许范围。",
  "Compare the proposed WPS values—not just their nominal settings—with that envelope.": "把拟用 WPS 的数值，而不只是名义设定，与该范围逐项比较。",
  "Check whether production can measure and record the stated range.": "确认生产现场能够测量并记录所规定的范围。",
  "Escalate any change outside the range before welding; do not convert it into an informal site deviation.": "任何超出范围的变更都应在焊接前升级处理，不得变成非正式的现场偏差。",
  "Properties can narrow a formally valid range": "性能要求可能缩小形式上有效的范围",
  "Impact testing temperature, HAZ hardness, weld-metal toughness, high-strength steel heat-input limits and project-specific CTOD requirements can make the practically usable range narrower than the maximum permitted by the generic qualification table. The project specification may also require Level 2 testing or additional specimens.": "冲击试验温度、热影响区硬度、焊缝金属韧性、高强钢热输入限值和项目特定 CTOD 要求，都可能使实际可用范围小于通用评定表允许的最大范围。项目规范还可能要求 Level 2 试验或附加试样。",
  "A valid WPQR is evidence. Applicability is a separate engineering check performed against the production joint.": "有效的 WPQR 是证据；适用性则是针对生产接头另行进行的工程审查。",

  "CTOD measures resistance to crack-tip deformation under a defined test condition. It is useful when a real flaw and stress state must be assessed—not simply because a plate is “thick.”": "CTOD 测量材料在规定试验条件下抵抗裂纹尖端变形的能力。它适用于需要评估真实缺陷和应力状态的情况，而不是仅仅因为钢板“很厚”。",
  "What the test measures": "试验测量什么",
  "Crack-tip opening displacement is a fracture-toughness parameter. In an ISO 15653 weld test, a notched specimen is fatigue precracked so that the crack tip samples a target weld-metal or HAZ microstructure. The specimen is then loaded at a defined temperature. The result describes resistance to crack initiation or extension under the test geometry and constraint.": "裂纹尖端张开位移是一项断裂韧度参数。在 ISO 15653 焊接试验中，带缺口试样通过疲劳预制裂纹，使裂纹尖端取样目标焊缝金属或热影响区组织，随后在规定温度下加载。结果描述材料在该试样几何和拘束条件下抵抗裂纹起始或扩展的能力。",
  "Why HAZ testing is difficult": "为什么热影响区试验很困难",
  "The HAZ is narrow and heterogeneous. A fatigue precrack intended for coarse-grained HAZ may pass through weld metal, fine-grained HAZ or parent steel. After testing, metallographic sectioning is needed to show which microstructure the crack front actually sampled. A numerically valid test can still be irrelevant to the target zone.": "热影响区狭窄且不均匀。原本希望位于粗晶热影响区的疲劳预裂纹，可能穿过焊缝金属、细晶热影响区或母材。试验后需要进行金相剖切，以确认裂纹前缘实际取样了哪种组织。即使数值上有效的试验，也可能与目标区域无关。",
  "CTOD is not a fatigue-life test": "CTOD 不是疲劳寿命试验",
  "Fatigue cycling is used to create a sharp precrack, but the CTOD test evaluates fracture resistance during subsequent loading. Fatigue assessment instead needs a cyclic stress range, detail category or crack-growth model. The two analyses can interact in an ECA—fatigue may grow a flaw to a final size—but they answer different questions.": "疲劳循环用于形成尖锐预裂纹，但 CTOD 试验评估的是随后加载过程中的抗断裂能力。疲劳评估则需要循环应力范围、细节类别或裂纹扩展模型。两类分析可以在 ECA 中相互关联，例如疲劳可能使缺陷扩展至最终尺寸，但它们回答的是不同问题。",
  "When testing is valuable": "何时进行试验才有价值",
  "A highly stressed or highly restrained welded detail operates at low temperature.": "高应力或高拘束焊接细节在低温下工作。",
  "A project proposes acceptance of a known planar flaw larger than workmanship limits.": "项目拟接受一个超过工艺验收限值的已知平面缺陷。",
  "Failure consequence is high and Charpy energy alone does not represent the required fracture model.": "失效后果严重，且仅凭夏比冲击功不能代表所需断裂模型。",
  "A new material, thickness, weld metal or heat-input range lacks relevant fracture data.": "新的材料、厚度、焊缝金属或热输入范围缺乏相关断裂数据。",
  "An engineering critical assessment requires project-specific toughness input.": "工程临界评估需要项目特定的韧性输入。",
  "Why there is no universal CTOD pass value": "为什么不存在通用的 CTOD 合格值",
  "A value such as 0.15 mm or 0.20 mm has no universal meaning without test temperature, crack location, specimen thickness, constraint, loading rate and the assessment method. Required toughness is calculated from applied and residual stresses, flaw size and orientation, geometry, material strength, temperature and safety factors. Different structures can therefore require different values from the same steel.": "如果不说明试验温度、裂纹位置、试样厚度、拘束、加载速率和评估方法，0.15 mm 或 0.20 mm 之类的数值没有通用意义。所需韧性应根据施加应力和残余应力、缺陷尺寸与方向、几何、材料强度、温度和安全系数计算。因此，同一种钢材用于不同结构时可能需要不同数值。",
  "How CTOD supports an ECA": "CTOD 如何支持 ECA",
  "Define the failure mode, service temperature, load history and consequence.": "明确失效模式、使用温度、载荷历程和后果。",
  "Characterise the flaw: height, length, orientation, location and sizing uncertainty.": "表征缺陷：高度、长度、方向、位置和定量不确定性。",
  "Determine stress—including local concentration and residual stress—at the flaw.": "确定缺陷处应力，包括局部应力集中和残余应力。",
  "Use tensile data representative of the assessed region and temperature.": "采用能够代表评估区域和温度的拉伸数据。",
  "Obtain fracture toughness from correctly located, representative specimens.": "从位置正确且具有代表性的试样获得断裂韧度。",
  "Apply the chosen failure-assessment procedure and sensitivity checks.": "应用选定的失效评估程序并进行敏感性检查。",
  "Translate the result into inspection capability, acceptance limits and monitoring requirements.": "把结果转化为检测能力、验收限值和监测要求。",
  "Not an automatic 40 mm rule": "不是自动适用的 40 mm 规则",
  "Thickness affects constraint and can be a trigger in a project specification, but no cross-code rule says every weld at or above 40 mm requires CTOD. The trigger comes from the contract, application standard, design risk or ECA strategy.": "厚度会影响拘束，也可能成为项目规范中的触发条件，但不存在跨规范通用规则，规定所有厚度达到或超过 40 mm 的焊缝都必须进行 CTOD。触发条件来自合同、应用标准、设计风险或 ECA 策略。",
  "First define the flaw assessment. Then specify the toughness test that supplies its missing input.": "应先定义缺陷评估，再规定用于提供缺失输入的韧性试验。",
  "The ECA method, safety factors and required inputs must be agreed for the project; CTOD testing alone does not establish allowable flaw size.": "ECA 方法、安全系数和所需输入必须在项目中达成一致；单独进行 CTOD 试验不能确定允许缺陷尺寸。",

  "A hardness traverse is a map of local response across a welded joint. Its value comes from the test layout and governing acceptance rule—not from quoting 350, 380 or 450 HV in isolation.": "焊接接头硬度横向测量是一张局部响应分布图。它的价值来自试验布置和适用验收规则，而不是孤立地引用 350、380 或 450 HV。",
  "What hardness reveals": "硬度能反映什么",
  "Vickers hardness correlates broadly with local strength and microstructure. A sharp HAZ peak can indicate fast cooling and a hard transformation product; a trough can reveal tempering or softening in quenched-and-tempered steel. Hardness is therefore useful in procedure qualification and failure investigation, but it is not a direct measurement of toughness, ductility or hydrogen content.": "维氏硬度与局部强度和显微组织大体相关。热影响区的尖锐硬度峰可能表示快速冷却和硬化转变产物；低谷则可能反映调质钢中的回火或软化。因此，硬度对工艺评定和失效调查很有用，但它并不是韧性、延性或氢含量的直接测量。",
  "Test method matters": "试验方法很重要",
  "ISO 9015-1 covers hardness testing on cross-sections of arc-welded joints, commonly using HV5 or HV10. The load, surface preparation, indentation spacing, test-line position and distance from surfaces must be reported. Results from different loads or layouts should not be compared as if they were identical.": "ISO 9015-1 涵盖电弧焊接头横截面的硬度试验，通常采用 HV5 或 HV10。报告必须说明载荷、表面制备、压痕间距、测线位置以及与表面的距离。不同载荷或布置得到的结果不能当作完全相同的数据进行比较。",
  "Where to place indentations": "压痕应布置在哪里",
  "Use sufficient points in parent metal, HAZ and weld metal to show the profile.": "在母材、热影响区和焊缝金属中设置足够测点，以显示完整分布。",
  "Place HAZ indentations close enough to capture the narrow peak or softened region without violating minimum spacing rules.": "热影响区压痕应足够接近，以捕捉狭窄硬度峰或软化区，同时不得违反最小间距规定。",
  "For multipass welds, consider cap, mid-thickness and root traverses because reheating differs.": "对于多道焊，应考虑盖面、中厚度和根部测线，因为各处再热情况不同。",
  "For dissimilar joints, sample both parent steels and both HAZs.": "对于异种接头，应测量两侧母材和两侧热影响区。",
  "Record a macrograph with the traverse locations; a list of numbers without location has limited value.": "记录标有测线位置的宏观照片；没有位置的一列数字价值有限。",
  "Why a high value can matter": "为什么高硬度可能重要",
  "High local hardness may indicate a microstructure more susceptible to hydrogen-assisted cracking, particularly when diffusible hydrogen and tensile stress are present. The relationship depends on steel type and service environment. A hardness value does not cause cracking on its own, and a value below a remembered threshold does not prove immunity.": "局部高硬度可能表示组织更容易发生氢致裂纹，尤其是在扩散氢和拉应力同时存在时。这种关系取决于钢种和服役环境。硬度值本身不会造成开裂，低于记忆中的某个阈值也不能证明不会开裂。",
  "Why a low value can matter": "为什么低硬度也可能重要",
  "In Q&T and some TMCP steels, welding can create a softened HAZ. If the soft zone is wide and highly stressed, it can affect joint strength or deformation. A maximum-hardness criterion alone misses this issue; the reviewer should consider minimum hardness, zone width, transverse tensile behaviour and structural demand.": "在调质钢和某些 TMCP 钢中，焊接可能形成软化热影响区。如果软化区较宽且承受高应力，就可能影响接头强度或变形。仅采用最高硬度准则会漏掉这一问题；审查人员还应考虑最低硬度、软化区宽度、横向拉伸行为和结构需求。",
  "Where the acceptance value comes from": "验收值从哪里来",
  "The application standard, material group, service environment and project specification define acceptance. Limits used for sour service, pressure equipment or a particular procedure qualification cannot automatically be imported into a building or bridge project. ISO 9015-1 tells the laboratory how to test; it does not create one universal pass/fail value for every material.": "应用标准、材料组别、服役环境和项目规范共同定义验收要求。用于含硫服役、压力设备或某项特定工艺评定的限值，不能自动移用于建筑或桥梁项目。ISO 9015-1 告诉实验室如何试验，但不会为所有材料建立一个通用合格／不合格数值。",
  "A useful report contains": "一份有效报告应包括",
  "Material identity, thickness, delivery condition and weld procedure.": "材料身份、厚度、交货状态和焊接工艺。",
  "Test method, load, equipment and calibration status.": "试验方法、载荷、设备和校准状态。",
  "Macrograph with every traverse and indentation location.": "标有每条测线和每个压痕位置的宏观照片。",
  "Individual readings—not only a maximum.": "每个单独读数，而不只是最大值。",
  "Applicable acceptance clause and any project modification.": "适用验收条款及任何项目修改。",
  "Comment on both hard peaks and softened zones.": "同时评述硬度峰和软化区。",
  "The correct question is not “Is it below 350 HV?” but “What limit applies to this material, service and qualification route—and did the traverse sample the critical microstructure?”": "正确的问题不是“是否低于 350 HV？”，而是“什么限值适用于这种材料、服役条件和评定路线？测线是否取样了关键显微组织？”",

  "A method standard explains how to examine. A quality level classifies imperfections. An acceptance standard decides which indications pass. Mixing those jobs produces ambiguous inspection plans.": "方法标准说明如何检测，质量等级对焊接缺欠进行分级，验收标准决定哪些显示可以接受。混淆这些职责会产生含糊的检验计划。",
  "Start with the governing application": "从适用工程规范开始",
  "The contract and execution specification establish the structural code, execution class, weld category, extent of examination and required quality. Under European steelwork practice, EN 1090-2 connects execution requirements to the project specification. ISO 17635 provides general rules for selecting NDT methods and evaluating results. Neither should be reduced to a single “percentage NDT” remembered from another project.": "合同和施工规范确定结构规范、施工等级、焊缝类别、检测范围和所需质量。在欧洲钢结构实践中，EN 1090-2 把施工要求与项目规范联系起来；ISO 17635 则提供选择无损检测方法和评价结果的一般规则。两者都不能被简化成从其他项目记住的某个“无损检测百分比”。",
  "ISO 5817: workmanship quality levels": "ISO 5817：制造质量等级",
  "ISO 5817 defines quality levels B, C and D for geometric imperfections in fusion-welded joints, with B the most stringent. It covers imperfections such as cracks, lack of fusion, porosity, undercut and excess weld metal under defined conditions. A quality level describes workmanship; it does not by itself prove fatigue resistance, fracture safety or fitness for service.": "ISO 5817 为熔化焊接头的几何缺欠规定 B、C、D 三个质量等级，其中 B 最严格。它在规定条件下涵盖裂纹、未熔合、气孔、咬边和焊缝金属过多等缺欠。质量等级描述制造质量，但本身不能证明疲劳抗力、断裂安全性或适用性。",
  "Method and testing level": "检测方法与检测等级",
  "Method": "方法",
  "Strong application": "适用优势",
  "Important limitation": "重要限制",
  "Surface profile, dimensions, undercut, visible cracks and misalignment": "表面轮廓、尺寸、咬边、可见裂纹和错边",
  "Requires access, lighting, cleaning and suitable gauges": "需要可达性、照明、清洁和合适量具",
  "Surface and near-surface cracks in ferromagnetic steel": "铁磁性钢材的表面和近表面裂纹",
  "Direction-sensitive and not suitable for non-ferromagnetic materials": "具有方向敏感性，不适用于非铁磁材料",
  "Surface-breaking imperfections in non-porous materials": "非多孔材料中的表面开口缺欠",
  "Cannot detect buried flaws; rough or coated surfaces reduce reliability": "不能检测埋藏缺陷；粗糙或有涂层表面会降低可靠性",
  "Internal planar flaws and through-thickness location": "内部平面缺陷及其厚度方向位置",
  "Coverage depends on geometry, procedure, calibration and qualified personnel": "覆盖能力取决于几何、程序、校准和合格人员",
  "Volumetric flaws and a permanent image": "体积型缺陷和永久影像记录",
  "Planar flaws can be missed when orientation is unfavourable": "方向不利时可能漏检平面缺陷",
  "A testing level defines how thoroughly a method is applied—scan coverage, sensitivity or technique. It is not the same as an acceptance level. PAUT is not automatically “better UT”; the written procedure must define probes, wedges, focal laws, coverage, reference sensitivity, data storage and evaluation.": "检测等级规定某种方法实施到什么程度，包括扫描覆盖、灵敏度或技术要求。它与验收等级不同。PAUT 并不会自动成为“更好的 UT”；书面程序必须规定探头、楔块、聚焦法则、覆盖范围、参考灵敏度、数据存储和评价方法。",
  "Acceptance level": "验收等级",
  "The method-specific acceptance standard converts indications into pass/fail rules. ISO 17635 gives relationships and selection principles, but the mapping is not a universal one-to-one conversion for every method and imperfection. The inspection plan should name the method standard, testing level and acceptance standard separately.": "特定检测方法的验收标准把显示转换为合格／不合格规则。ISO 17635 给出相互关系和选择原则，但这种对应并不是适用于每种方法和每类缺欠的通用一一转换。检验计划应分别写明方法标准、检测等级和验收标准。",
  "A clear ITP line item": "一条清晰的 ITP 项目",
  "Weld population → extent → timing → method → testing level → acceptance level → responsible person → record": "焊缝总体 → 检测比例 → 检测时机 → 方法 → 检测等级 → 验收等级 → 责任人 → 记录",
  "“10% UT to ISO 5817 B” is incomplete: ISO 5817 is not a UT procedure, and the statement does not define how the sample is selected, when it is tested or what happens after rejection. A usable ITP also defines lot formation, random or risk-based selection, expansion rules, delayed inspection and repair re-examination.": "“按 ISO 5817 B 级进行 10% UT”是不完整的：ISO 5817 不是 UT 检测程序，而且该表述没有说明如何抽样、何时检测或出现不合格后如何处理。可执行的 ITP 还应规定批次划分、随机或基于风险的选择、扩大检测规则、延迟检测和修补后复检。",
  "Do not mix code systems silently": "不要在没有说明的情况下混用规范体系",
  "AWS D1.1 contains its own inspection and acceptance framework. An ISO method may be used only when the contract establishes how it relates to AWS acceptance. Selecting the most convenient clause from each system after an indication is found destroys the agreed acceptance basis.": "AWS D1.1 有其自身的检验和验收框架。只有当合同明确规定 ISO 方法与 AWS 验收之间的关系时，才能采用 ISO 方法。发现显示后再从不同体系中挑选最方便的条款，会破坏双方约定的验收依据。",
  "Every NDT report should let a reviewer answer: what was examined, how thoroughly, against which acceptance rule, and with what result?": "每份无损检测报告都应让审查人员回答：检测了什么、检测到什么程度、依据哪项验收规则，以及结果如何？",

  "The Hong Kong Steel Code treats inspection as part of a controlled fabrication route: approved procedures, qualified personnel, defined timing, appropriate NDT and records that remain traceable to the weld.": "香港钢结构规范把检验视为受控制造流程的一部分，包括经批准的工艺、合格人员、明确的检测时机、适当的无损检测，以及始终可追溯到具体焊缝的记录。",
  "Identify the correct project regime": "识别正确的项目规范体系",
  "Building works governed by the Buildings Department’s Code of Practice for the Structural Use of Steel are not the same contractual regime as CEDD public works using the General Specification for Civil Engineering Works. A project may also invoke EN/ISO or AWS documents. The specification must state which requirement governs each design, fabrication and inspection activity.": "受屋宇署《钢结构使用守则》管辖的建筑工程，与采用《土木工程一般规格》的土木工程拓展署公共工程并不属于同一合同体系。项目还可能引用 EN/ISO 或 AWS 文件。规范必须说明每项设计、制造和检验活动由哪项要求控制。",
  "Procedure approval comes before production": "生产前必须完成工艺批准",
  "Section 14 of the Steel Code requires welding procedure specifications to be submitted before work starts and connects procedure testing with witnessed examination, mechanical tests, parent-material certificates and carbon-equivalent records. A welder qualification does not replace a qualified WPS, and a qualified WPS does not replace welder or operator qualification.": "《钢结构规范》第 14 节要求在开工前提交焊接工艺规程，并把工艺试验与见证检验、力学试验、母材证书和碳当量记录联系起来。焊工资格不能替代经评定的 WPS，经评定的 WPS 也不能替代焊工或操作工资格。",
  "Visual examination is the first layer": "目视检验是第一层控制",
  "Every weld should be visually examined for profile, size, surface condition and obvious imperfections before supplementary NDT. VT also confirms that the surface and geometry are suitable for MT, PT, UT or RT. Final acceptance should reference the project-adopted criteria rather than an inspector’s personal workmanship preference.": "每条焊缝在补充无损检测前，都应通过目视检验检查外形、尺寸、表面状态和明显缺欠。VT 还用于确认表面和几何是否适合 MT、PT、UT 或 RT。最终验收应引用项目采用的准则，而不是检验员个人对制造质量的偏好。",
  "Why delayed NDT matters": "为什么延迟无损检测很重要",
  "Hydrogen cracks can appear after the weld cools. The Steel Code provides a delay framework related to carbon equivalent and combined thickness, with a general minimum delay and additional consideration for higher-strength material. It is inaccurate to replace that framework with a universal “always wait 24 hours” or “always wait 48 hours.” The clock, applicable weld population and restart after repair should be defined in the ITP.": "氢致裂纹可能在焊缝冷却后出现。《钢结构规范》提供了与碳当量和组合厚度相关的延迟框架，包括一般最低延迟时间和对较高强度材料的额外考虑。用“始终等待 24 小时”或“始终等待 48 小时”的通用说法替代该框架并不准确。起算时间、适用焊缝总体以及修补后的重新计时方式都应在 ITP 中明确。",
  "High-strength steel requires deliberate coverage": "高强钢需要有针对性的检测覆盖",
  "For steels above 500 MPa yield strength, the Code sets a strong expectation of 100% NDT unless another arrangement is agreed by the Responsible Engineer under the applicable provision. When strength exceeds the range covered by the prescriptive delay table, the inspection timing should be established with appropriate welding expertise rather than extrapolated casually.": "对于屈服强度超过 500 MPa 的钢材，规范明确倾向于要求 100% 无损检测，除非责任工程师依据适用条款同意其他安排。当强度超出规定性延迟表所覆盖的范围时，应由具备适当焊接专业能力的人员确定检测时机，而不能随意外推。",
  "Parent-plate UT and lamellar-tearing zones": "母材 UT 与层状撕裂区域",
  "Thick T- and cruciform joints can impose through-thickness shrinkage strain. The Code calls attention to ultrasonic examination of parent plate around critical attachment zones—particularly for plate over 25 mm in relevant details—and to re-examination after welding. The drawing and ITP should define the zone, method, acceptance and traceability before fabrication.": "厚板 T 形和十字接头可能产生厚度方向收缩应变。规范特别关注关键附件区域周围母材的超声检测，尤其是相关构造中厚度超过 25 mm 的钢板，并要求焊后重新检测。图纸和 ITP 应在制造前明确检测区域、方法、验收和可追溯性。",
  "A traceable inspection record": "可追溯的检验记录",
  "Material heat → cut-piece ID → assembly → weld ID → WPS/welder → parameters → NDT → repair → re-test → as-built": "材料炉号 → 下料件编号 → 装配 → 焊缝编号 → WPS／焊工 → 参数 → 无损检测 → 修补 → 复检 → 竣工记录",
  "Link every weld report to a drawing or weld map location.": "把每份焊缝报告关联到图纸或焊缝图上的位置。",
  "Record process, WPS, welder/operator, date and relevant consumable batch.": "记录焊接方法、WPS、焊工／操作工、日期和相关焊材批次。",
  "State NDT procedure, equipment, calibration, personnel qualification, extent and acceptance clause.": "注明无损检测程序、设备、校准、人员资格、检测范围和验收条款。",
  "Maintain a nonconformance record for rejectable indications and recurring trends.": "对不可接受显示和重复出现的趋势保留不符合项记录。",
  "Use an approved repair procedure; re-examine the repaired and required adjacent area after the applicable delay.": "采用经批准的修补工艺，并在适用延迟时间后复检修补区及规定的邻近区域。",
  "Return the final status to the weld map and handover dossier.": "把最终状态更新回焊缝图和移交资料。",
  "The role of the Responsible Engineer": "责任工程师的作用",
  "Approval by the RE is a defined project control, not a substitute for technical evidence. Any reduced coverage, alternative method, deviation or concession should state its basis, scope and conditions. The latest Buildings Department amendments and project specification should be checked at the time of use.": "责任工程师批准是一项明确的项目控制措施，不能替代技术证据。任何降低检测比例、替代方法、偏差或让步，都应说明其依据、范围和条件。使用时应核查屋宇署最新修订和项目规范。",
  "Inspection is complete only when the result can be traced to the physical weld and every rejection has a closed disposition.": "只有当检验结果能够追溯到实体焊缝，且每个不合格项都已闭环处置时，检验才算完成。",
  "Check the contract edition, Buildings Department amendments and project-specific RE approval route before applying any numerical requirement.": "应用任何数值要求前，应核查合同规定版本、屋宇署修订以及项目特定的责任工程师批准路径。",
  "Carbon-equivalent formulae reduce chemical composition to an empirical index associated with hardenability and hydrogen-cracking susceptibility. They are inputs to a preheat assessment; they are not preheat temperatures, weldability certificates or universal acceptance limits.": "碳当量公式把化学成分归纳为与淬硬倾向及氢致裂纹敏感性相关的经验指标。碳当量是预热评估的输入参数，并不等同于预热温度、可焊性证明或通用验收限值。",
  "Common formulae": "常用公式",
  "Element contents are entered as mass percentages. The formulae were developed from different steel populations and welding datasets. CEV, CET and Pcm are therefore not interchangeable, even when they produce similar numerical values. The formula required by the adopted assessment method must be used.": "各元素含量均以质量百分数代入。这些公式基于不同钢种范围和焊接数据建立，因此即使 CEV、CET 与 Pcm 的计算值相近，也不能相互替代；应采用所选评估方法规定的公式。",
  "Engineering meaning": "工程含义",
  "For comparable ferritic steels, a higher carbon-equivalent value generally indicates a greater potential for hard transformation products when the heat-affected zone cools rapidly. The value is useful for comparing heats, checking the composition represented by a qualified procedure and selecting the appropriate preheat-assessment method. It does not describe the thermal cycle or the completed joint.": "对于具有可比性的铁素体钢，碳当量越高，热影响区快速冷却时形成硬化转变组织的可能性通常越大。该指标可用于比较不同炉次、核查生产材料成分是否处于已评定工艺所代表的范围内，以及选择合适的预热评估方法；但它不能描述实际热循环或完工接头的性能。",
  "Additional inputs to preheat assessment": "预热评估所需的其他输入",
  "Input factor": "输入因素",
  "Reason it is required": "需要考虑的原因",
  "Diffusible-hydrogen level": "扩散氢水平",
  "Depends on the welding process, consumable classification, conditioning and exposure": "取决于焊接方法、焊接材料等级、处理状态及暴露情况",
  "Combined thickness and joint geometry": "组合厚度与接头几何",
  "Control the heat sink and cooling rate around the weld": "控制焊缝周围的散热条件和冷却速度",
  "Heat input, preheat and interpass temperature": "热输入、预热温度与道间温度",
  "Determine the temperature-time cycle with the joint geometry": "与接头几何共同决定温度—时间循环",
  "Restraint and stress concentration": "拘束与应力集中",
  "Affect the tensile stress acting while hydrogen redistributes": "影响氢重新分布期间作用的拉应力",
  "Steel product and delivery condition": "钢材产品与交货状态",
  "Q&T, TMCP and normalized products can respond differently at the same nominal strength": "相同名义强度下，调质、热机械轧制和正火产品的焊接响应可能不同",
  "Fixed CEV thresholds": "固定 CEV 阈值的局限",
  "A statement such as “CEV below 0.40 means that preheat is unnecessary” is not a complete engineering rule. A thin, low-restraint joint made with controlled low-hydrogen consumables may require no intentional preheat, while a thick or highly restrained joint from the same heat may require preheat. Tack welds, attachments and repairs can also present more severe local cooling or restraint than the principal production weld.": "“CEV 低于 0.40 即无需预热”并不是完整的工程判据。采用受控低氢焊接材料的薄板、低拘束接头可能无需专门预热，而同一炉次钢材用于厚板或高拘束接头时可能需要预热。定位焊、附件焊和返修焊的局部冷却或拘束条件也可能比主体生产焊缝更严苛。",
  "EN-based review sequence": "以 EN 标准为主的审查顺序",
  "Identify the exact steel product, delivery condition, thickness and ladle analysis from the inspection document.": "依据检验文件确认钢材的准确产品牌号、交货状态、厚度和熔炼分析。",
  "Use the carbon-equivalent formula required by the governing method.": "采用适用评估方法规定的碳当量公式。",
  "Assign the hydrogen scale from qualified welding-consumable data and the actual handling procedure.": "根据经评定的焊接材料数据及实际保管、烘干和领用程序确定氢含量等级。",
  "Define combined thickness, joint geometry, heat input, restraint, initial temperature and environmental condition.": "明确组合厚度、接头几何、热输入、拘束、初始温度和环境条件。",
  "Apply the project-adopted EN 1011-2 method and check any more restrictive product-manufacturer limits.": "采用项目指定的 EN 1011-2 方法，并核查产品制造商提出的更严格限制。",
  "Confirm that the resulting preheat and interpass requirements lie within the qualified WPS range and can be measured during production.": "确认所得预热和道间温度要求处于 WPS 的评定范围内，并可在生产中实施测量。",
  "Carbon equivalent characterises composition. Preheat is determined from the interaction of composition, hydrogen, heat flow and restraint.": "碳当量表征化学成分；预热要求则由成分、氢、热流和拘束的共同作用确定。",
  "Use the assessment method and edition stated in the project specification. Product guidance does not replace procedure qualification.": "应采用项目规范规定的评估方法和标准版本。产品指南不能代替焊接工艺评定。",

  "The t8/5 parameter is the time taken for a weld thermal cycle to cool from 800 °C to 500 °C. For many ferritic steels, it is a useful descriptor of the cooling interval in which major austenite transformations occur.": "t8/5 是焊接热循环从 800 °C 冷却至 500 °C 所经历的时间。对许多铁素体钢而言，它可用于表征奥氏体主要转变发生阶段的冷却历程。",
  "Metallurgical significance": "冶金意义",
  "A short t8/5 generally increases the likelihood of hard transformation products; a long t8/5 generally favours softer products and allows more time at elevated temperature. The relationship is steel-specific. Continuous-cooling-transformation data are relevant only when the chemical composition, initial microstructure and austenitising cycle are representative of the product being welded.": "较短的 t8/5 通常会增加硬化转变组织形成的可能性；较长的 t8/5 通常有利于形成较软组织，并延长高温停留时间。这种关系具有钢种特异性。只有当化学成分、初始组织和奥氏体化循环能够代表实际焊接产品时，连续冷却转变数据才具有适用性。",
  "Thermal variables": "热过程变量",
  "Arc energy or calculated heat input does not uniquely determine t8/5. Heat flow also depends on joint geometry, effective thickness, bead dimensions, preheat, interpass temperature and the position of the pass in a multipass sequence.": "电弧能量或计算热输入不能唯一决定 t8/5。热流还取决于接头几何、有效厚度、焊道尺寸、预热温度、道间温度以及该焊道在多道焊顺序中的位置。",
  "Typical effect, subject to joint geometry": "典型影响（仍受接头几何制约）",
  "Usually lengthens t8/5": "通常延长 t8/5",
  "Higher arc energy or heat input": "较高的电弧能量或热输入",
  "Larger effective heat sink": "更大的有效散热体",
  "Can shorten t8/5 at the same welding parameters": "在相同焊接参数下可能缩短 t8/5",
  "Start, stop and short-bead regions": "起弧、收弧与短焊道区域",
  "Create transient cycles not represented by steady-state calculations": "形成稳态计算不能反映的瞬态热循环",
  "Multipass welding": "多道焊",
  "Reheats existing HAZ and produces intercritically or subcritically reheated regions": "使原有热影响区再次受热，形成临界间或亚临界再热区域",
  "Heat-affected-zone sub-regions": "热影响区的分区",
  "the peak temperature is sufficiently high for substantial prior-austenite grain growth; toughness can be reduced.": "峰值温度足以引起显著的原奥氏体晶粒长大，韧性可能降低。",
  "the region is fully austenitised at a lower peak temperature and generally develops a finer prior-austenite grain size.": "该区域在较低峰值温度下完全奥氏体化，通常形成较细的原奥氏体晶粒。",
  "only part of the microstructure is austenitised; local softening or brittle constituents can occur depending on the steel and reheating cycle.": "仅部分组织发生奥氏体化；是否出现局部软化或脆性组分取决于钢种和再热循环。",
  "no re-austenitisation occurs, but tempering can reduce hardness and strength in quenched-and-tempered steel.": "不发生再奥氏体化，但回火作用可能降低调质钢的硬度和强度。",
  "Upper and lower process limits": "工艺上限与下限",
  "A lower limit on the qualified thermal input can be required to avoid rapid cooling, excessive hardness and increased susceptibility to hydrogen-assisted cold cracking. An upper limit can be required to control coarse-grained HAZ toughness, HAZ width and softening. The acceptable interval is specific to the product, thickness, joint and property requirements; it is not a generic value attached to “S690” or “S960”.": "为避免冷却过快、硬度过高和氢致冷裂纹敏感性增加，可能需要对经评定的热输入规定下限；为控制粗晶热影响区韧性、热影响区宽度和软化，也可能需要规定上限。允许区间取决于具体产品、厚度、接头和性能要求，并不是附属于“S690”或“S960”的通用数值。",
  "Use in procedure development": "在工艺开发中的应用",
  "Obtain product-specific t8/5 or heat-input guidance where it is available.": "如有资料，应取得针对具体产品的 t8/5 或热输入指南。",
  "Estimate the cooling time for the actual joint geometry, effective thickness and initial temperature.": "按实际接头几何、有效厚度和初始温度估算冷却时间。",
  "Make the procedure test with representative welding parameters, bead size and pass sequence.": "采用具有代表性的焊接参数、焊道尺寸和焊接顺序进行工艺评定试验。",
  "Locate hardness, tensile and impact tests so that the relevant HAZ regions are assessed.": "合理布置硬度、拉伸和冲击试验，使相关热影响区得到评价。",
  "Convert the acceptable test conditions into measurable WPS limits for current, voltage, travel speed, bead dimensions, preheat and maximum interpass temperature.": "把可接受的试验条件转化为 WPS 中可测量的电流、电压、焊接速度、焊道尺寸、预热温度和最高道间温度限值。",
  "Assess tack welds, attachments, starts, stops and repairs separately where their thermal cycles are more severe.": "当定位焊、附件焊、起弧、收弧和返修焊的热循环更严苛时，应分别评估。",
  "t8/5 is a thermal-cycle parameter, not a material property. Its allowable range must be supported by the actual product and procedure qualification.": "t8/5 是热循环参数，不是材料性能。其允许范围必须由实际产品和焊接工艺评定提供依据。",

  "Weld cracking": "焊接裂纹",
  "WELD CRACKING": "焊接裂纹",
  "Hydrogen-assisted cold cracking requires the combined presence of diffusible hydrogen, a susceptible local microstructure and tensile stress during a critical temperature-time interval. Control measures must address all of these conditions.": "氢致冷裂纹需要扩散氢、敏感的局部组织和拉应力在临界温度—时间区间内共同存在。控制措施必须同时针对这些条件。",
  "Diffusible hydrogen": "扩散氢",
  "Moisture in covered electrodes or flux, contaminated wire, damp joint surfaces, coatings, oil and inadequate shielding-gas control can introduce hydrogen to the weld pool. The relevant measure is diffusible hydrogen in deposited weld metal, not total hydrogen. A low-hydrogen consumable classification remains valid in production only when storage, re-drying where applicable, issue time and exposure are controlled.": "焊条药皮或焊剂中的水分、受污染的焊丝、潮湿接头表面、涂层、油污以及保护气体控制不当，都可能把氢带入熔池。相关指标是熔敷金属中的扩散氢，而不是总氢。只有对储存、必要时的再烘干、领用时间和暴露条件实施控制，低氢焊接材料等级才能在生产中保持有效。",
  "Microstructural susceptibility": "组织敏感性",
  "Rapid cooling can produce high-hardness transformation products in the HAZ. Susceptibility depends on composition, delivery condition, prior microstructure and the local weld thermal cycle; carbon equivalent and t8/5 are therefore supporting parameters rather than acceptance criteria. Cracking can also occur in high-strength weld metal, so an HAZ hardness result alone does not establish freedom from hydrogen cracking.": "快速冷却可能在热影响区形成高硬度转变组织。敏感性取决于化学成分、交货状态、原始组织和局部焊接热循环，因此碳当量和 t8/5 是辅助参数，而不是验收准则。裂纹也可能出现在高强焊缝金属中，所以仅凭热影响区硬度结果不能证明不会发生氢致裂纹。",
  "Tensile stress and restraint": "拉应力与拘束",
  "Weld shrinkage generates residual tensile stress without external loading. Thick tee and cruciform joints, attachments, closed frames, short repairs and poorly planned sequences can impose high restraint. Root imperfections and abrupt weld profiles add local stress concentration. The restraint in a production detail can therefore be more severe than that in a procedure-test plate.": "即使没有外载，焊接收缩也会产生残余拉应力。厚板 T 形和十字接头、附件、封闭框架、短段返修焊以及不合理的焊接顺序都可能造成高拘束。根部缺欠和突变的焊缝外形还会增加局部应力集中，因此实际生产构造的拘束可能比工艺评定试板更严苛。",
  "Delayed formation and inspection": "延迟形成与检测时机",
  "Hydrogen redistribution continues as the joint cools, and cracking can occur after welding is complete. Final NDT performed too early may not reveal delayed cracks. The minimum hold time must be taken from the governing fabrication code or project specification and should reflect material strength, combined thickness, carbon equivalent, heat input and restraint.": "接头冷却过程中氢仍会继续重新分布，裂纹可能在焊接完成后才形成。过早进行最终无损检测可能无法发现延迟裂纹。最短等待时间必须取自适用制造规范或项目规范，并应反映材料强度、组合厚度、碳当量、热输入和拘束条件。",
  "Integrated prevention": "综合预防",
  "Primary function": "主要作用",
  "Limitation": "局限",
  "Low-hydrogen consumables and clean, dry joints": "低氢焊接材料及清洁、干燥的接头",
  "Reduce available diffusible hydrogen": "减少可扩散氢",
  "Do not remove hard microstructure or restraint": "不能消除硬化组织或拘束",
  "Preheat and controlled interpass temperature": "预热及受控道间温度",
  "Modify cooling and allow more time for hydrogen diffusion": "调整冷却过程并为氢扩散提供更多时间",
  "Must remain within product and WPS limits": "必须保持在产品和 WPS 限值内",
  "Controlled arc energy, bead size and sequence": "受控的电弧能量、焊道尺寸和焊接顺序",
  "Control the local thermal cycle and restraint development": "控制局部热循环和拘束的形成",
  "Cannot compensate for wet consumables": "不能弥补焊接材料受潮",
  "Joint detailing and fit-up": "接头构造与装配",
  "Reduce restraint and stress concentration": "降低拘束和应力集中",
  "Do not remove material susceptibility": "不能消除材料敏感性",
  "Increase the probability of detecting delayed cracking": "提高发现延迟裂纹的概率",
  "Detection is not prevention": "检测不能代替预防",
  "Dehydrogenation heat treatment": "消氢处理",
  "A controlled post-weld dehydrogenation treatment can maintain the joint at an elevated temperature to promote hydrogen effusion. It is not equivalent to stress-relief post-weld heat treatment. The temperature, holding time and transfer from welding must be qualified for the actual steel. An unqualified generic treatment can temper quenched-and-tempered material and reduce parent-metal or HAZ properties.": "受控的焊后消氢处理可使接头在较高温度下保持一段时间，促进氢逸出。它不等同于消除应力焊后热处理。处理温度、保温时间以及从焊接结束到处理的转移时间必须针对实际钢材进行评定。未经评定而套用通用处理，可能使调质材料发生回火，降低母材或热影响区性能。",
  "Failure investigation": "失效调查",
  "Locate the crack relative to weld metal, fusion boundary and HAZ.": "确定裂纹相对于焊缝金属、熔合线和热影响区的位置。",
  "Establish the time of discovery and review consumable batches, issue records and environmental conditions.": "确认裂纹发现时间，并复核焊接材料批次、领用记录和环境条件。",
  "Reconstruct actual heat input, preheat, interpass temperature, bead placement and sequence.": "还原实际热输入、预热温度、道间温度、焊道布置和焊接顺序。",
  "Assess hardness, microstructure, fracture morphology and restraint together.": "综合评估硬度、显微组织、断口形貌和拘束。",
  "Do not infer the cracking mechanism from elemental analysis alone.": "不要仅凭元素分析推断开裂机理。",
  "Before repair, remove the causal condition and approve the excavation, preheat and repair-welding procedure.": "返修前应消除致因，并批准缺陷清除、预热和返修焊工艺。",
  "Hydrogen-assisted cold cracking is controlled by the welding system; no single carbon-equivalent or hardness value demonstrates immunity.": "氢致冷裂纹必须通过焊接体系进行控制；任何单一碳当量或硬度数值都不能证明材料绝对免疫。",

  "Welding procedure qualification": "焊接工艺评定",
  "The applicable code system must be identified before the documents are reviewed. ISO uses pWPS, WPS and WPQR; AWS uses WPS and PQR. Similar abbreviations do not make the qualification routes interchangeable.": "审查文件前必须先明确适用的规范体系。ISO 体系使用 pWPS、WPS 和 WPQR；AWS 体系使用 WPS 和 PQR。缩写相近并不表示两种评定路线可以互换。",
  "Document sequence under the ISO procedure-test route": "ISO 工艺评定试验路线下的文件顺序",
  "pWPS → qualification test weld → examination and testing → WPQR → production WPS": "pWPS → 工艺评定试件焊接 → 检验与试验 → WPQR → 生产用 WPS",
  "ISO 15609-1 specifies the content of an arc-welding WPS. ISO 15614-1 specifies one route for qualifying a preliminary WPS by a welding procedure test and defines the resulting range of qualification. The WPQR records the actual test conditions, examination and test results, and the range derived from the applicable qualification standard.": "ISO 15609-1 规定电弧焊 WPS 的内容。ISO 15614-1 规定通过焊接工艺评定试验评定预焊接工艺规程的一种路线，并确定由此得到的评定范围。WPQR 记录实际试验条件、检验与试验结果，以及按适用评定标准确定的范围。",
  "Function of each document": "各文件的作用",
  "Document": "文件",
  "Function": "作用",
  "Information that must remain traceable": "必须保持可追溯的信息",
  "Instructions used to produce the qualification test weld": "用于施焊工艺评定试件的工艺要求",
  "Joint preparation, parent materials, welding process, consumables, position, parameters and thermal controls": "接头制备、母材、焊接方法、焊接材料、焊接位置、参数和热过程控制",
  "Record of the qualification test and its results": "工艺评定试验及其结果的记录",
  "Actual materials, actual welding variables, NDT, destructive tests, deviations and the calculated qualification range": "实际材料、实际焊接变量、无损检测、破坏性试验、偏差及计算得到的评定范围",
  "Controlled instruction for production welding": "受控的生产焊接工艺文件",
  "Permitted values or ranges, sequence, consumable control, preheat, interpass temperature and any post-weld treatment": "允许值或范围、焊接顺序、焊接材料控制、预热温度、道间温度及焊后处理",
  "Actual values and permitted ranges": "实际值与允许范围",
  "A qualification record must state the values actually used for the test weld. If the measured current was 245 A, recording a broad machine range such as 200–300 A does not describe the test. A production WPS can contain a range only where that range is supported by the governing qualification rules and remains technically suitable for the production joint.": "评定记录必须注明试件焊接时实际采用的数值。例如实测电流为 245 A，仅记录 200–300 A 之类的设备宽泛范围并不能描述该试验。只有在适用评定规则支持且技术上适合实际生产接头时，生产用 WPS 才能规定相应范围。",
  "Applicability to the production weld": "对生产焊缝的适用性",
  "A signed WPQR or PQR is not sufficient by itself. The production WPS must be checked against the qualified parent-material grouping, product form, thickness, deposited weld-metal thickness, pipe diameter where relevant, joint type, welding process, position, backing, consumables, heat input or arc-energy controls, preheat, interpass temperature and post-weld heat treatment. The comparison is made against the code edition stated in the contract.": "仅有一份已签署的 WPQR 或 PQR 并不足够。必须核对生产用 WPS 是否处于已评定的母材组别、产品形式、厚度、熔敷焊缝金属厚度、适用时的管径、接头形式、焊接方法、焊接位置、衬垫、焊接材料、热输入或电弧能量控制、预热温度、道间温度和焊后热处理范围内。核对应以合同规定的规范版本为准。",
  "ISO, GB/T and AWS are separate systems": "ISO、GB/T 与 AWS 是不同的规范体系",
  "ISO 15614-1 and AWS D1.1 use different qualification rules and terminology. AWS D1.1 also permits prequalified WPSs, but only when every applicable condition of that code is satisfied. An AWS prequalified WPS is not an ISO pWPS, and an ISO WPQR does not automatically qualify an AWS WPS.": "ISO 15614-1 与 AWS D1.1 采用不同的评定规则和术语。AWS D1.1 也允许采用免除评定的 WPS，但前提是满足该规范所有适用条件。AWS 的免除评定 WPS 不是 ISO 的 pWPS，ISO 的 WPQR 也不会自动使 AWS WPS 获得资格。",
  "For Chinese terminology, GB/T 19867.1-2005 uses “焊接工艺规程” for WPS, and GB/T 19869.1-2005 covers welding procedure qualification tests. Both remain current in China at the time of writing, but they adopt earlier ISO editions. They should not be treated as textually identical to ISO 15609-1:2019 or ISO 15614-1:2017+A1:2019.": "在中文术语方面，GB/T 19867.1—2005 将 WPS 称为“焊接工艺规程”，GB/T 19869.1—2005 规定焊接工艺评定试验。撰写本文时两项标准在中国均为现行标准，但等同采用的是较早版本的 ISO 标准，不能视为与 ISO 15609-1:2019 或 ISO 15614-1:2017+A1:2019 逐字一致。",
  "Minimum document-control check": "文件控制的最低核查要求",
  "Confirm the governing code, edition and qualification route.": "确认适用规范、版本和评定路线。",
  "Match material certificates and consumable records to the qualification test piece.": "核对材料证书、焊接材料记录与工艺评定试件的对应关系。",
  "Verify that actual welding variables were recorded contemporaneously.": "确认实际焊接变量在施焊过程中同步记录。",
  "Check that NDT, specimen locations and laboratory reports identify the same test weld.": "确认无损检测、试样位置和实验室报告均指向同一评定焊缝。",
  "Derive the range of qualification from the applicable standard; do not copy it from an unrelated certificate.": "按适用标准确定评定范围，不得从无关证书照抄。",
  "Issue the production WPS with a unique number, revision, approval status and link to the relevant WPQR/PQR.": "生产用 WPS 应具有唯一编号、修订号和批准状态，并关联相应 WPQR/PQR。",
  "The WPQR or PQR establishes qualification evidence. The WPS converts that evidence into controlled production instructions.": "WPQR 或 PQR 提供工艺评定证据；WPS 把这些证据转化为受控的生产焊接工艺要求。",
  "Use the standard and edition invoked by the contract. A national adoption may correspond to an earlier ISO edition.": "应采用合同指定的标准及版本；国家标准的采用版本可能对应较早的 ISO 版本。",

  "Carbon Equivalent in Preheat Assessment": "预热评估中的碳当量",
  "t8/5 Cooling Time and Heat-Affected-Zone Response": "t8/5 冷却时间与热影响区响应",
  "Hydrogen-Assisted Cold Cracking in High-Strength Steel": "高强钢氢致冷裂纹",
  "WPS, pWPS and WPQR/PQR: Document Roles and Control": "WPS、pWPS 与 WPQR/PQR：文件作用及控制",
  "Qualification applies to a defined range of welding conditions. Under ISO 15614-1 the controlling concept is the range of qualification; “essential variables” is the established AWS terminology and should not be imposed on the ISO route without qualification.": "工艺评定仅适用于明确的焊接条件范围。ISO 15614-1 的核心概念是“评定范围”；“重要变素”是 AWS 体系的既定术语，不应不加说明地套用于 ISO 评定路线。",
  "Start from the production joint": "从生产接头开始核查",
  "The review begins with the production material, product form, dimensions, joint, welding process, position and required properties. Those conditions are compared with the recorded test conditions and the range permitted by the governing standard. A company name or certificate cover sheet does not establish coverage.": "审查应从生产用材料、产品形式、尺寸、接头、焊接方法、焊接位置和所需性能开始，再将这些条件与评定记录中的试验条件及适用标准允许的范围逐项比较。公司名称或证书封面本身不能证明评定覆盖。",
  "Variable groups requiring verification": "需要核查的变量组",
  "Variable group": "变量组",
  "Typical items": "典型项目",
  "Parent material": "母材",
  "Material group and subgroup, product form, grade, delivery condition and dissimilar combination": "材料组别和分组、产品形式、牌号、交货状态及异种材料组合",
  "Dimensions": "尺寸",
  "Parent-material thickness, deposited weld-metal thickness and outside diameter where applicable": "母材厚度、熔敷焊缝金属厚度，以及适用时的外径",
  "ISO 4063 reference number, process sequence, degree of mechanisation and transfer mode where applicable": "ISO 4063 方法编号、焊接方法顺序、机械化程度，以及适用时的熔滴过渡形式",
  "Joint and position": "接头与焊接位置",
  "Butt or fillet weld, penetration, backing, gouging, root technique and welding position": "对接焊缝或角焊缝、熔透情况、衬垫、清根、根部工艺及焊接位置",
  "Welding consumables": "焊接材料",
  "Classification and designation, diameter, flux-wire combination and shielding or backing gas": "分类与型号、直径、焊剂—焊丝组合以及保护气体或背面保护气体",
  "Thermal conditions": "热过程条件",
  "Arc energy or heat input, minimum preheat temperature, maximum interpass temperature and post-weld heat treatment": "电弧能量或热输入、最低预热温度、最高道间温度及焊后热处理",
  "Qualification level under ISO 15614-1": "ISO 15614-1 的评定等级",
  "ISO 15614-1:2017 provides Level 1 and Level 2 procedure tests. Level 2 requires more extensive testing and gives more restrictive qualification ranges. A Level 2 test qualifies Level 1 requirements, but not conversely. If neither the contract nor the application standard specifies a level, ISO 15614-1 requires Level 2.": "ISO 15614-1:2017 规定 1 级和 2 级工艺评定试验。2 级要求更多试验，并给出更严格的评定范围。2 级试验可覆盖 1 级要求，反之则不成立。合同和应用标准均未指定等级时，ISO 15614-1 要求采用 2 级。",
  "Thickness is only one qualification dimension": "厚度只是评定范围的一个维度",
  "A thicker test piece does not automatically cover every production weld. For example, a change from process 135 to process 136, a change in parent-material group, the addition or removal of backing, or a different process sequence can fall outside the qualified range. The exact effect must be taken from the applicable tables and clauses; it should not be inferred from general welding experience.": "采用更厚的试件并不意味着自动覆盖所有生产焊缝。例如，焊接方法由 135 改为 136、母材组别改变、增加或取消衬垫，或改变焊接方法顺序，都可能超出评定范围。其具体影响必须依据适用表格和条款确定，不能凭一般焊接经验推断。",
  "Formal range and engineering suitability": "规范评定范围与工程适用性",
  "Remaining inside a formal qualification range is necessary but may not be sufficient. Impact-test temperature, weld-metal toughness, hardness, hydrogen control, maximum interpass temperature, product-specific heat-input limits and project CTOD requirements can narrow the usable WPS range. This is particularly important for quenched-and-tempered and thermomechanically rolled high-strength steels.": "处于规范规定的评定范围内是必要条件，但可能仍不充分。冲击试验温度、焊缝金属韧性、硬度、氢控制、最高道间温度、产品特定热输入限值和项目 CTOD 要求，都可能进一步收窄 WPS 的可用范围；这对调质及热机械轧制高强钢尤其重要。",
  "Change-control review": "变更控制审查",
  "List each production variable and the required property in a controlled comparison sheet.": "在受控对照表中列出每项生产变量和所需性能。",
  "Record the actual WPQR/PQR test values and results.": "记录 WPQR/PQR 的实际试验数值和结果。",
  "Derive the permitted range from the stated code and edition.": "依据指定规范及版本确定允许范围。",
  "Confirm that every production WPS value lies inside that range.": "确认生产用 WPS 的每个数值均处于该范围内。",
  "Check any additional restrictions from the execution specification, product manufacturer and design basis.": "核查施工技术规范、产品制造商和设计依据提出的附加限制。",
  "Refer an out-of-range change for formal disposition before welding; do not treat it as an undocumented shop adjustment.": "超出范围的变更必须在施焊前提交正式处置，不得作为无记录的车间调整。",
  "Qualification range is a code-defined boundary. Suitability is the engineering assessment that the WPS will deliver the required joint properties within that boundary.": "评定范围是规范界定的边界；适用性则是工程判断，即 WPS 能否在该边界内获得所需接头性能。",
  "Do not transfer qualification ranges between ISO, national adoptions and AWS unless the contract establishes an accepted route.": "除非合同明确规定认可路线，否则不得在 ISO、国家采用标准与 AWS 体系之间直接转移评定范围。",

  "S960 identifies a nominal strength level, not a complete material specification. Welding requirements must be based on the product standard, grade suffix, delivery condition, thickness, joint configuration and required joint properties.": "S960 表示名义强度等级，并不是完整的材料技术条件。焊接要求必须依据产品标准、牌号后缀、交货状态、厚度、接头构造和所需接头性能确定。",
  "Product identification": "产品识别",
  "S960 products are available under different product standards and delivery routes. For example, quenched-and-tempered plate grades under EN 10025-6 and thermomechanically rolled cold-forming grades under EN 10149-2 are not metallurgically interchangeable. The inspection document and manufacturer’s product data must therefore be reviewed before a welding procedure is selected.": "S960 产品可按不同产品标准和交货路线供应。例如，EN 10025-6 的调质钢板牌号与 EN 10149-2 的热机械轧制冷成形钢牌号在冶金上不能互换。因此，选择焊接工艺前必须审查检验文件和制造商产品资料。",
  "Lower thermal limit": "热过程下限",
  "Low arc energy, a large heat sink and low initial temperature can shorten t8/5 and produce high-hardness HAZ microstructures. Hydrogen-assisted cold-cracking susceptibility then depends on diffusible hydrogen and restraint as well as cooling rate. The lower procedural limit is therefore established from product composition, combined thickness, joint geometry, preheat, consumable hydrogen level and restraint.": "较低电弧能量、较大散热体和较低初始温度会缩短 t8/5，并可能形成高硬度热影响区组织。此时氢致冷裂纹敏感性除受冷却速度影响外，还取决于扩散氢和拘束。因此，工艺下限应结合产品成分、组合厚度、接头几何、预热、焊接材料氢含量等级和拘束确定。",
  "Upper thermal limit": "热过程上限",
  "High arc energy or excessive interpass temperature can lengthen the thermal cycle, widen the HAZ and increase grain growth or tempering. In quenched-and-tempered steel, intercritical and subcritical HAZ regions may soften relative to the delivered plate. The structural significance depends on the soft-zone width, joint geometry, weld-metal mismatch and stress state; a hardness minimum or tensile test may be needed in addition to a maximum-hardness check.": "较高电弧能量或过高道间温度会延长热循环、扩大热影响区，并加剧晶粒长大或回火。调质钢的临界间和亚临界热影响区可能相对交货状态钢板发生软化。其结构影响取决于软化区宽度、接头几何、焊缝金属强度匹配和应力状态；除最高硬度检查外，还可能需要规定最低硬度或进行拉伸试验。",
  "Variables defining the qualified window": "界定评定窗口的变量",
  "Technical relevance": "技术意义",
  "Product, delivery condition and thickness": "产品、交货状态与厚度",
  "Define chemistry, initial microstructure, specified properties and heat sink": "确定化学成分、初始组织、规定性能及散热条件",
  "Joint geometry and bead placement": "接头几何与焊道布置",
  "Control local heat flow and reheating of earlier passes": "控制局部热流及先前焊道的再热",
  "Welding process and consumable": "焊接方法与焊接材料",
  "Affect arc-energy transfer, deposited-metal properties and diffusible hydrogen": "影响电弧能量传递、熔敷金属性能和扩散氢",
  "Control cooling rate and accumulated thermal exposure": "控制冷却速度和累积热作用",
  "Preheat and interpass temperature": "预热温度与道间温度",
  "Required joint properties": "所需接头性能",
  "Determine the necessary tensile, impact, hardness, fatigue or fracture evidence": "确定所需拉伸、冲击、硬度、疲劳或断裂性能证据",
  "Procedure-development sequence": "工艺开发顺序",
  "Verify the exact product designation, delivery condition, thickness range and inspection document.": "核实准确的产品牌号、交货状态、厚度范围和检验文件。",
  "Review product-manufacturer limits and the project’s EN/ISO or other governing requirements.": "审查产品制造商限值以及项目采用的 EN/ISO 或其他适用要求。",
  "Select compatible low-hydrogen welding consumables with appropriate strength and impact properties at the design temperature.": "选择相容的低氢焊接材料，并确保其强度和设计温度下的冲击性能适当。",
  "Set preliminary limits for preheat, maximum interpass temperature, arc energy or heat input, bead dimensions and sequence.": "初步设定预热、最高道间温度、电弧能量或热输入、焊道尺寸和顺序的限值。",
  "Qualify the actual material combination, joint type, thickness and process sequence.": "对实际材料组合、接头形式、厚度和焊接方法顺序进行评定。",
  "Assess transverse tensile strength and fracture location, impact properties where specified, hardness distribution and HAZ softening.": "评价横向拉伸强度及断裂位置、规定时的冲击性能、硬度分布和热影响区软化。",
  "Transfer only the supported range to the production WPS and verify that production can monitor it.": "只把有证据支持的范围转入生产用 WPS，并确认生产过程能够监控。",
  "Fanling North application": "粉岭北工程应用",
  "Public information from The Hong Kong Polytechnic University describes the development of S960 box-girder welding technology using testing and numerical simulation for different plate thicknesses and joint designs, followed by application to factory-fabricated footbridge girders. The transferable lesson is the qualification approach, not a single heat-input value: product, joint geometry, thermal cycle and measured joint performance were considered together.": "香港理工大学公开资料介绍了针对不同板厚和接头设计，结合试验与数值模拟开发 S960 箱梁焊接技术，并将其应用于工厂预制的人行天桥梁段。可借鉴的是这种评定思路，而不是某个单一热输入数值：应把产品、接头几何、热循环和实测接头性能综合考虑。",
  "The inspection document establishes the delivered plate properties. Procedure qualification establishes evidence for the welded joint within a defined range.": "检验文件证明钢板交货状态下的性能；焊接工艺评定则为规定范围内的焊接接头提供性能证据。",

  "A Z designation verifies reduction of area in the through-thickness direction. It reduces material susceptibility but does not by itself prevent lamellar tearing; joint geometry, weld shrinkage and restraint remain controlling design variables.": "Z 向等级验证材料厚度方向的断面收缩率。它可降低材料敏感性，但不能单独防止层状撕裂；接头几何、焊接收缩和拘束仍是主要设计控制因素。",
  "Mechanism": "形成机理",
  "Rolling can elongate non-metallic inclusions parallel to the plate surface. When weld contraction or service load imposes through-thickness strain, separation can develop between inclusion arrays. Lamellar tearing is typically a stepped crack in the parent material, approximately parallel to the rolled surface and commonly adjacent to highly restrained tee, corner or cruciform welds.": "轧制可使非金属夹杂沿平行于钢板表面的方向延伸。当焊接收缩或服役载荷产生厚度方向应变时，夹杂带之间可能发生分离。层状撕裂通常表现为母材中的阶梯状裂纹，大致平行于轧制表面，常见于高拘束 T 形、角接或十字接头焊缝附近。",
  "EN 10164 classes": "EN 10164 等级",
  "EN 10164:2018 specifies improved deformation properties perpendicular to the product surface. The Z class is based on reduction of area in a through-thickness tensile test; it is neither a sulfur-content class nor a direct percentage probability of avoiding tearing.": "EN 10164:2018 规定产品表面法向的改善变形性能。Z 向等级以厚度方向拉伸试验的断面收缩率为依据；它既不是硫含量等级，也不表示避免层状撕裂的直接概率百分数。",
  "Minimum average reduction of area": "最小平均断面收缩率",
  "Minimum individual result": "最小单个试验结果",
  "For Z35, the specified average is 35% and the individual minimum is 25%; it is incorrect to require every result to reach 35% unless the purchase specification adds that condition. EN 10164 applies principally to fully killed steel products within its stated thickness and strength scope. Product eligibility must be checked before ordering.": "对于 Z35，规定平均值为 35%，单个试验结果最小值为 25%；除非采购技术条件另有规定，要求每个结果均达到 35% 是不正确的。EN 10164 主要适用于其规定厚度和强度范围内的全镇静钢产品，订货前必须核查产品适用性。",
  "Details with elevated susceptibility": "敏感性较高的构造",
  "Large single-sided fillet or partial-penetration welds deposited on the face of thick plate.": "在厚板表面施焊的大尺寸单面角焊缝或部分熔透焊缝。",
  "Tee, corner and cruciform joints that transmit weld shrinkage through the plate thickness.": "把焊接收缩传递到钢板厚度方向的 T 形、角接和十字接头。",
  "Highly restrained nodes and details with excessive weld volume.": "高拘束节点及焊缝体积过大的构造。",
  "Poor fit-up that increases weld size or creates uneven shrinkage.": "导致焊缝尺寸增大或收缩不均的装配不良。",
  "Attachments close to plate edges or regions with local segregation.": "靠近板边或局部偏析区域的附件。",
  "Design controls": "设计控制",
  "The preferred control is to reduce or redirect through-thickness strain. Measures include reorienting the plate, changing the load path, reducing weld volume, balancing the welding sequence and using a joint detail that permits in-plane deformation. Buttering can alter the shrinkage path or reduce restraint, but the material, thickness and sequence require procedure qualification.": "优先控制措施是减小厚度方向应变或改变其传递方向。可采用调整钢板方向、改变传力路径、减小焊缝体积、平衡焊接顺序以及选用允许面内变形的接头构造。堆焊隔离层可改变收缩路径或降低拘束，但其材料、厚度和施焊顺序需要进行工艺评定。",
  "Z-quality and ultrasonic testing": "Z 向性能与超声检测",
  "Z-quality is specified when the design assessment identifies through-thickness strain demand that cannot be removed by detailing. Selection should follow the adopted design method, including the relevant EN 1993-1-10 provisions where applicable. Parent-material UT can identify laminations or loss of back-wall response in critical zones, but it does not measure through-thickness ductility and cannot replace a specified Z class.": "当设计评估识别出无法通过构造措施消除的厚度方向应变需求时，应规定 Z 向性能。等级选择应遵循项目采用的设计方法，适用时包括 EN 1993-1-10 的相关规定。母材超声检测可发现关键区域的分层或底波衰减，但不能测量厚度方向延性，也不能替代规定的 Z 向等级。",
  "GB/T 5313-2023 is the current Chinese product standard for steel plate with through-thickness properties. It provides the appropriate Chinese terminology—“厚度方向性能”和“断面收缩率”—but the purchase specification must still state the governing product standard and class rather than assume automatic equivalence with EN 10164.": "GB/T 5313—2023 是中国现行的《厚度方向性能钢板》产品标准，并采用“厚度方向性能”和“断面收缩率”等规范术语。但采购技术条件仍须明确适用产品标准和等级，不能假定其与 EN 10164 自动等效。",
  "Design and fabrication review": "设计与制造审查",
  "Identify where weld shrinkage and service stress act through the product thickness.": "识别焊接收缩和服役应力沿产品厚度方向作用的位置。",
  "Assess restraint, weld volume, product thickness and consequence of cracking.": "评估拘束、焊缝体积、产品厚度及开裂后果。",
  "Improve the joint detail before increasing the Z class.": "提高 Z 向等级前，应先改进接头构造。",
  "Select the required through-thickness class using the governing design method.": "按适用设计方法选择所需厚度方向性能等级。",
  "Specify any parent-material UT zone, method and acceptance criterion before fabrication.": "制造前规定母材超声检测区域、方法和验收准则。",
  "Maintain material identity and plate orientation after cutting.": "下料后保持材料标识和钢板方向的可追溯性。",
  "A Z class is evidence of through-thickness ductility; it is not a substitute for a sound joint detail.": "Z 向等级是厚度方向延性的证据，不能代替合理的接头构造。",

  "Welding consumables": "焊接材料",
  "WELDING CONSUMABLES": "焊接材料",
  "Welding-consumable selection must be based on the design resistance, deformation demand, toughness, service temperature, diffusible-hydrogen requirement and procedure-qualification evidence. Parent-steel grade alone is not a complete selection rule.": "焊接材料的选择必须以设计承载力、变形需求、韧性、服役温度、扩散氢要求和工艺评定证据为依据。仅凭母材钢级不能构成完整的选择规则。",
  "Definition of matching": "匹配的定义",
  "“Matching” may refer to specified yield strength, specified tensile strength or measured properties of a particular heat. Those bases can give different mismatch classifications. A consumable classification normally states minimum all-weld-metal properties under prescribed test conditions; production weld-metal properties also depend on dilution, shielding gas, arc energy, bead sequence and cooling rate.": "“等强匹配”可能以规定屈服强度、规定抗拉强度或某一炉次的实测性能为比较基础，不同基础可能得出不同的匹配分类。焊接材料分类通常给出规定试验条件下的全焊缝金属最低性能；实际生产焊缝金属性能还取决于稀释、保护气体、电弧能量、焊道顺序和冷却速度。",
  "Strength-selection strategies": "强度选择策略",
  "Strategy": "策略",
  "Engineering objective": "工程目标",
  "Required verification": "所需验证",
  "Matching": "等强匹配",
  "Provide nominal weld-metal strength comparable with the governing parent material": "使焊缝金属名义强度与控制设计的母材相当",
  "Confirm the comparison basis and actual procedure-test results": "确认比较基础及实际工艺评定试验结果",
  "Overmatching": "超强匹配",
  "Promote plastic deformation away from the weld metal in a highly utilised butt joint": "使高利用率对接接头的塑性变形倾向于避开焊缝金属",
  "Verify weld-metal toughness, ductility, hydrogen control and HAZ response": "验证焊缝金属韧性、延性、氢控制及热影响区响应",
  "Undermatching": "低匹配",
  "Reduce alloy demand or provide a controlled deformation location where design permits": "在设计允许时降低合金化需求或提供受控变形位置",
  "Demonstrate joint resistance and deformation capacity; do not adopt by assumption": "必须证明接头承载力和变形能力，不得凭假设采用",
  "Structural design and consumable classification": "结构设计与焊接材料分类",
  "The structural design standard determines the resistance of the weld and connected parts. The selected consumable and WPS must then deliver the properties assumed in that calculation. A fillet-weld resistance check based on the weaker connected material does not, by itself, specify the filler-metal classification. Impact properties, service temperature, fatigue category, dilution, coating or backing materials and the qualification route remain relevant.": "结构设计标准确定焊缝及被连接构件的承载力；所选焊接材料和 WPS 必须能够实现计算所假定的性能。按较弱被连接材料进行角焊缝承载力验算，本身并不能确定填充金属分类。冲击性能、服役温度、疲劳类别、稀释、涂层或衬垫材料以及评定路线仍需考虑。",
  "High-strength-steel considerations": "高强钢的特殊考虑",
  "High-strength steel considerations": "高强钢的特殊考虑",
  "As strength increases, it becomes more difficult to combine high weld-metal strength with adequate toughness and low diffusible hydrogen. Overmatched weld metal can transfer strain to a softened HAZ, while deliberately undermatched weld metal can localise strain in the weld. Either condition requires assessment of joint geometry, mismatch, loading mode and the applicable ultimate, fatigue or fracture limit state.": "随着强度提高，同时获得高焊缝金属强度、足够韧性和低扩散氢更加困难。超强匹配焊缝金属可能把应变转移至软化热影响区，有意采用的低匹配焊缝金属则可能使应变集中在焊缝。两种情况都需要评估接头几何、强度失配、加载方式以及适用的承载、疲劳或断裂极限状态。",
  "Identify the governing connected component and design limit state.": "确定控制设计的被连接构件和设计极限状态。",
  "Verify the product standards, delivery conditions, thickness-dependent properties and design temperature of both parent materials.": "核实两侧母材的产品标准、交货状态、随厚度变化的性能和设计温度。",
  "Specify the required weld-metal yield or tensile strength basis, impact class and hydrogen designation.": "规定焊缝金属所需的屈服或抗拉强度基础、冲击等级和氢含量标识。",
  "Consider dilution from both parent materials and any metallic backing or coating.": "考虑两侧母材以及任何金属衬垫或涂层造成的稀释。",
  "Review transverse tensile strength and fracture location, weld-metal impact results where required, hardness distribution and HAZ softening.": "审查横向拉伸强度及断裂位置、规定时的焊缝金属冲击结果、硬度分布和热影响区软化。",
  "Selection statement": "选材说明",
  "A technically complete selection statement identifies the governing code, parent materials and thicknesses, design temperature, required consumable classification, diffusible-hydrogen designation, WPS/WPQR reference and any additional impact, hardness or CTOD requirement. “Use the strongest available filler” is not a specification.": "技术上完整的选材说明应列明适用规范、母材及厚度、设计温度、所需焊接材料分类、扩散氢标识、WPS/WPQR 编号，以及任何附加冲击、硬度或 CTOD 要求。“采用可获得的最高强度填充材料”并不是技术规范。",
  "The appropriate weld-metal strength is the strength supported by the design basis and qualification evidence—not necessarily the highest available classification.": "合适的焊缝金属强度应由设计依据和评定证据支持，并不一定是可获得的最高强度等级。",

  "Welding Procedure Qualification: Variables and Range of Qualification": "焊接工艺评定：变量与评定范围",
  "Welding S960: Defining and Qualifying the Thermal Window": "S960 焊接：热循环窗口的确定与评定",
  "Through-Thickness Properties and Lamellar Tearing": "厚度方向性能与层状撕裂",
  "Weld-Metal Strength Matching in High-Strength Steel Joints": "高强钢接头的焊缝金属强度匹配",
  "The assessment method, safety factors and required inputs must be agreed for the project; CTOD testing alone does not establish allowable flaw size.": "评定方法、安全系数和所需输入必须在项目中约定；仅凭 CTOD 试验不能确定允许缺陷尺寸。",
  "An engineering critical assessment requires project-specific toughness input.": "工程临界评定需要项目特定的韧度输入。",
  "CTOD Testing and Engineering Critical Assessment": "CTOD 试验与工程临界评定",
  "A CTOD test measures fracture toughness under a defined test condition. An engineering critical assessment uses toughness together with flaw, stress and geometry data to judge fitness for service. The test is an input to the assessment, not the assessment itself.": "CTOD 试验测定规定试验条件下的断裂韧度。工程临界评定综合采用韧度、缺陷、应力和几何数据判断结构的适用性。试验只是评定的输入，而不是评定本身。",
  "Apply the selected assessment procedure, such as the project-adopted edition of BS 7910, with the specified safety factors and sensitivity checks.": "采用选定的评定程序，例如项目指定版本的 BS 7910，并按规定采用安全系数和进行敏感性分析。",
  "Hardness Testing of Welded Joints": "焊接接头硬度试验",
  "A hardness traverse maps local response across a welded joint. It is meaningful only when the indentation positions, test load and governing acceptance requirement are stated; an isolated value such as 350 HV is not a universal limit.": "硬度测线用于表征焊接接头各局部区域的响应。只有明确压痕位置、试验力和适用验收要求时，结果才有意义；350 HV 之类的单一数值并不是通用限值。",
  "A weld-quality level, an NDT testing level and an NDT acceptance level are related, but they perform different functions. An inspection requirement is incomplete unless the governing application standard, examination method, testing level, acceptance standard, extent and timing are all stated.": "焊缝质量等级、无损检测的检测等级和验收等级彼此相关，但功能不同。只有同时明确适用的应用标准、检测方法、检测等级、验收标准、检测范围和时机，检验要求才完整。",
  "Hierarchy of requirements": "要求的层级关系",
  "The contract and execution specification establish the applicable structural code, execution class or weld category, required weld quality and extent of examination. For European structural steelwork, EN 1090-2 provides execution requirements and refers to the relevant EN ISO welding and NDT standards. ISO 17635 gives general rules for selecting NDT methods, techniques and acceptance levels; it does not replace the project execution specification.": "合同和施工技术规范确定适用的结构规范、施工等级或焊缝类别、所需焊缝质量及检测范围。对于欧洲钢结构工程，EN 1090-2 规定施工要求，并引用相关 EN ISO 焊接与无损检测标准。ISO 17635 给出选择无损检测方法、技术和验收等级的一般规则，但不能替代项目施工技术规范。",
  "Quality level under ISO 5817": "ISO 5817 的质量等级",
  "ISO 5817:2023 specifies quality levels B, C and D for imperfections in fusion-welded joints, with B representing the highest requirement on the finished weld. These are workmanship quality levels. ISO 5817 does not define an ultrasonic scan plan, radiographic technique or a universal fitness-for-service criterion. Metallurgical properties such as hardness and grain size are outside its scope.": "ISO 5817:2023 规定熔化焊接头缺欠的 B、C、D 三个质量等级，其中 B 级对完工焊缝的要求最高。这些是制造质量等级。ISO 5817 不规定超声扫描方案、射线检测技术或通用适用性评定准则；硬度和晶粒度等冶金性能不在其范围内。",
  "Method, testing level and acceptance standard": "检测方法、检测等级与验收标准",
  "Purpose": "用途",
  "Typical EN ISO document": "典型 EN ISO 文件",
  "What it controls": "控制内容",
  "Ultrasonic testing": "超声检测",
  "Technique, testing level and evaluation of manual UT for fusion welds": "熔化焊焊缝手工超声检测的技术、检测等级和评价",
  "UT acceptance": "超声检测验收",
  "Acceptance levels for ultrasonic indications": "超声显示的验收等级",
  "Magnetic particle testing": "磁粉检测",
  "MT technique / acceptance levels for indications": "磁粉检测技术／显示的验收等级",
  "Penetrant testing": "渗透检测",
  "PT principles / acceptance levels for indications": "渗透检测基本原则／显示的验收等级",
  "Radiographic testing": "射线检测",
  "Film or digital technique / acceptance levels for steel, nickel and titanium welds": "胶片或数字成像技术／钢、镍和钛焊缝的验收等级",
  "A testing level defines the rigour of the examination technique, including coverage and sensitivity. An acceptance level sets limits for relevant indications. ISO 17635:2025 states that NDT acceptance levels cannot be interpreted as a direct, one-to-one translation of ISO 5817 quality levels for every indication.": "检测等级规定检测技术的严格程度，包括覆盖范围和灵敏度；验收等级则对相关显示规定限值。ISO 17635:2025 指出，不能把无损检测验收等级理解为对 ISO 5817 质量等级中每一种显示的直接一一对应转换。",
  "Terminology in Chinese standards": "中国标准中的术语",
  "The corresponding Chinese technical terms are “缺欠” (imperfection), “显示” (indication), “检测等级” (testing level) and “验收等级” (acceptance level). GB/T 34628-2017 is the current Chinese adoption of ISO 17635:2016, while ISO 17635 has since been revised in 2025. For ultrasonic testing, GB/T 11345-2023 is identical to ISO 17640:2018, and GB/T 29712-2023 is identical to ISO 11666:2018. The adopted edition must therefore be stated rather than assuming that every GB/T document is identical to the latest ISO edition.": "对应的中文规范术语为“缺欠”（imperfection）、“显示”（indication）、“检测等级”（testing level）和“验收等级”（acceptance level）。GB/T 34628—2017 是 ISO 17635:2016 的中国现行等同采用标准，而 ISO 17635 已于 2025 年修订。超声检测方面，GB/T 11345—2023 等同采用 ISO 17640:2018，GB/T 29712—2023 等同采用 ISO 11666:2018。因此必须注明所采用版本，不能假定所有 GB/T 文件均与最新 ISO 版本一致。",
  "Content of an inspection and test plan": "检验和试验计划的内容",
  "Weld population → extent and selection → hold time → method → testing level → acceptance level → disposition → record": "焊缝总体 → 检测范围与抽样 → 等待时间 → 方法 → 检测等级 → 验收等级 → 处置 → 记录",
  "The instruction “10% UT to ISO 5817 B” is not technically complete. ISO 5817 is not a UT method standard, and the statement does not define the applicable UT technique, acceptance level, sample selection, hold time, expansion after rejection or re-examination after repair. Those items should be specified before fabrication begins.": "“按 ISO 5817 B 级进行 10% 超声检测”在技术上并不完整。ISO 5817 不是超声检测方法标准，该表述也没有规定适用的超声技术、验收等级、抽样方法、等待时间、不合格后的扩大检测或返修后的复检。这些内容应在制造开始前明确。",
  "Use of PAUT and mixed code systems": "相控阵超声检测及规范体系混用",
  "Phased-array ultrasonic testing is not accepted solely because it produces an encoded image. The written procedure must demonstrate coverage for the joint geometry and define probes, wedges, focal laws, reference sensitivity, calibration, data retention and evaluation. Where AWS D1.1 governs, its inspection and acceptance framework applies unless the contract formally establishes how an alternative ISO method and its results are to be used.": "相控阵超声检测不会仅因能够生成编码图像而自动获得认可。书面检测程序必须证明对接头几何的覆盖能力，并规定探头、楔块、聚焦法则、参考灵敏度、校准、数据保存和评价要求。当 AWS D1.1 为适用规范时，应采用其检验与验收框架，除非合同正式规定替代 ISO 方法及其结果的使用方式。",
  "An NDT report should identify the weld, examination extent, method and procedure, testing level, acceptance criterion, personnel, equipment, result and disposition.": "无损检测报告应明确焊缝、检测范围、方法与程序、检测等级、验收准则、人员、设备、结果和处置。",
  "Confirm the application standard and the exact edition of every referenced method and acceptance document.": "应确认应用标准以及每项引用检测方法和验收文件的准确版本。",
  "Weld NDT: Method, Testing Level and Acceptance Level": "焊缝无损检测：方法、检测等级与验收等级",

  "Section 14 of the Code of Practice for the Structural Use of Steel 2011 (2023 Edition) defines a fabrication-control route that includes procedure approval, personnel competence, visual inspection, NDT extent, hold time and traceable records. Its numerical requirements should be quoted by clause or table, not replaced by general rules of thumb.": "香港《钢结构使用守则 2011》（2023 年版）第 14 节规定了制造控制流程，包括工艺批准、人员能力、目视检验、无损检测范围、等待时间和可追溯记录。引用其中数值要求时应注明条款或表格，不应以一般经验规则替代。",
  "Confirm the governing project documents": "确认项目适用文件",
  "Buildings Department building works and CEDD public works do not necessarily use the same contractual requirements. The drawings, specification and inspection and test plan (ITP) should identify the governing Steel Code provisions and any supplementary EN ISO, AWS or project requirements. Where provisions differ, the contract must establish precedence.": "屋宇署监管的建筑工程与土木工程拓展署公共工程并不一定采用相同的合同要求。图纸、技术规范和检验与试验计划（ITP）应明确适用的《钢结构规范》条款，以及任何补充 EN ISO、AWS 或项目要求；如规定不一致，合同必须确定优先顺序。",
  "Welding procedures and personnel": "焊接工艺与人员",
  "Steel Code 14.3.3 requires welding procedure specifications to be submitted to the Responsible Engineer before welding starts. Procedure tests are to be witnessed, and the Code uses the term Welding Procedure Approval Record (WPAR). The record includes relevant material certificates, carbon-equivalent information, mechanical-test data and NDT results. Procedure approval and welder or welding-operator qualification are separate controls; neither replaces the other.": "《钢结构规范》14.3.3 要求在焊接开始前向负责工程师提交焊接工艺规程。工艺试验应接受见证，规范采用“焊接工艺批准记录”（WPAR）这一名称。记录包括相关材料证书、碳当量资料、力学试验数据和无损检测结果。工艺批准与焊工或焊接操作工资格是相互独立的控制，不能彼此替代。",
  "Visual inspection": "目视检验",
  "Clause 14.3.6.3 requires visual inspection over the full length of all welds before other required NDT. Welds that will become inaccessible are to be examined before access is lost. Visual inspection addresses dimensions, profile and visible surface imperfections and also establishes whether the surface is suitable for supplementary testing.": "第 14.3.6.3 条要求在其他规定无损检测前，对所有焊缝全长进行目视检验。将变得不可接近的焊缝应在失去可达性前完成检验。目视检验检查尺寸、外形和可见表面缺欠，并确认表面是否适合进行后续检测。",
  "Hold time before final NDT": "最终无损检测前的等待时间",
  "Clause 14.3.6.4 states that a hold time of at least 16 hours should generally be allowed before final inspection of as-welded fabrication. Table 14.2b then varies the typical hold time with IIW carbon equivalent and combined thickness. The Code also calls for reduction for some thin materials below 690 MPa yield strength and increase for combined thickness above 50 mm or yield strength above 690 MPa. High-restraint joints require particular consideration. A universal 24-hour or 48-hour rule is therefore not an accurate statement of the Code.": "第 14.3.6.4 条规定，焊态构件进行最终检验前通常应至少等待 16 小时。表 14.2b 再根据 IIW 碳当量和组合厚度调整典型等待时间。规范还规定，对某些屈服强度低于 690 MPa 的薄材可缩短时间，而组合厚度超过 50 mm 或屈服强度超过 690 MPa 时应延长；高拘束接头还需特别考虑。因此，把规范概括为统一等待 24 小时或 48 小时并不准确。",
  "The selected hold time is measured after completion of welding and is to be stated in the inspection record. Final surface-flaw detection and ultrasonic examination follow the applicable hold time. After repair, the project ITP should define when the hold-time period recommences.": "所选等待时间从焊接完成后起算，并应记录在检验记录中。最终表面缺陷检测和超声检测应在适用等待时间后进行。返修后，项目 ITP 应明确等待时间何时重新起算。",
  "NDT extent for high-strength steel": "高强钢的无损检测范围",
  "Table 14.3a defines mandatory NDT by weld type, orientation and thickness. Note 5 states that, for steel with yield strength greater than 500 N/mm², the testing frequency should be 100% unless otherwise agreed by the Responsible Engineer. Any reduction should therefore be a documented project decision supported by the applicable provision and production evidence.": "表 14.3a 按焊缝形式、方向和厚度规定强制无损检测。注 5 规定，对屈服强度大于 500 N/mm² 的钢材，除非负责工程师另行同意，检测频率应为 100%。因此，任何降低检测比例的决定都应形成项目记录，并有适用条款和生产证据支持。",
  "Parent-material ultrasonic testing": "母材超声检测",
  "Clause 14.3.5 requires, unless otherwise agreed by the Responsible Engineer, ultrasonic inspection before welding of material thicker than 25 mm in tee and cruciform connections within 150 mm of the weld. The inspector reports laminations and significant attenuation variations. This examination addresses parent-material integrity in a susceptible zone; it does not demonstrate through-thickness ductility and does not replace a specified Z-quality requirement.": "第 14.3.5 条规定，除非负责工程师另行同意，T 形和十字接头中厚度大于 25 mm 的材料，应在焊前对距焊缝 150 mm 范围内进行超声检测。检验人员应报告分层和明显的衰减变化。该检测用于评价敏感区域的母材完整性，不能证明厚度方向延性，也不能替代规定的 Z 向性能要求。",
  "Traceability and disposition": "可追溯性与处置",
  "Material certificate → cut-piece ID → weld ID → WPS/WPAR → welder → parameters → NDT → repair → re-examination → final status": "材料证书 → 下料件编号 → 焊缝编号 → WPS/WPAR → 焊工 → 参数 → 无损检测 → 返修 → 复检 → 最终状态",
  "Identify each report by drawing or weld-map location.": "通过图纸或焊缝图位置识别每份报告。",
  "Record the welding process, WPS, welder or operator, date and relevant consumable identification.": "记录焊接方法、WPS、焊工或操作工、日期及相关焊接材料标识。",
  "State the NDT procedure, equipment, calibration, personnel certification, extent and acceptance clause.": "注明无损检测程序、设备、校准、人员资格认证、检测范围和验收条款。",
  "Record rejectable indications as nonconformities and apply the specified expansion rules.": "把不可接受显示记录为不符合项，并执行规定的扩大检测规则。",
  "Use an approved repair procedure and re-examine the required repaired and adjacent zones.": "采用经批准的返修工艺，并对规定的返修区域和相邻区域进行复检。",
  "Close the disposition in the weld map and handover dossier.": "在焊缝图和移交资料中完成处置闭环。",
  "Responsible Engineer approval is a project control; it does not remove the need for a stated technical basis, defined scope and traceable record.": "负责工程师的批准是一项项目控制，并不能免除明确技术依据、界定适用范围和保留可追溯记录的要求。",
  "Clause references above are to the 2023 Edition. Confirm the contract edition, amendments and project-specific Responsible Engineer approval route before use.": "上述条款编号依据 2023 年版。使用前应确认合同版本、修订内容以及项目特定的负责工程师批准路径。",
  "Weld Inspection under the Hong Kong Steel Code": "香港《钢结构规范》下的焊缝检验",
  "Weld defects": "焊接缺陷",
  "Material selection": "材料选择",
  "Consumable selection": "焊材选择",
  "Procedure qualification": "工艺评定",
  "Fracture mechanics": "断裂力学",
  "Mechanical testing": "力学试验",
  "Non-destructive testing": "无损检测",
  "Hong Kong practice": "香港实践",

  "Q690qE is a bridge structural steel grade in GB/T 714-2025. Its name identifies a strength class, bridge-steel designation and impact-quality grade, but it does not by itself specify every property needed for procurement, design or welding.": "Q690qE 是 GB/T 714—2025 中的桥梁用结构钢牌号。该牌号表明强度等级、桥梁钢类别和冲击韧性质量等级，但不能单独规定采购、设计或焊接所需的全部性能。",
  "The four parts of the designation": "牌号的四个组成部分",
  "Symbol": "符号",
  "Meaning": "含义",
  "Initial letter of qu (屈), indicating yield strength": "“屈”字汉语拼音首字母，表示屈服强度",
  "Nominal yield-strength level in MPa. GB/T 714-2025 specifies a minimum of 690 MPa for nominal thickness up to 50 mm and 650 MPa for thickness over 50 mm up to 100 mm.": "以 MPa 表示的名义屈服强度等级。GB/T 714—2025 规定，公称厚度不大于 50 mm 时最小为 690 MPa，大于 50 mm 且不大于 100 mm 时最小为 650 MPa。",
  "Initial letter of qiao (桥), identifying bridge steel under GB/T 714": "“桥”字汉语拼音首字母，表示 GB/T 714 中的桥梁用钢",
  "Quality grade with Charpy V-notch impact testing at −40°C": "在 −40°C 进行夏比 V 型缺口冲击试验的质量等级",
  "For Q690q, the quality grades listed in GB/T 714-2025 are D, E and F, corresponding to Charpy test temperatures of −20°C, −40°C and −60°C respectively. Grade C is used for some lower-strength bridge steels in the same standard, but it is not a Q690q quality grade.": "GB/T 714—2025 规定的 Q690q 质量等级为 D、E 和 F，对应的夏比冲击试验温度分别为 −20°C、−40°C 和 −60°C。C 级用于该标准中部分较低强度桥梁钢，但不是 Q690q 的质量等级。",
  "Concise definition:": "简要定义：",
  "Q690qE is a Q690-strength-class bridge structural steel to GB/T 714-2025. The lowercase q identifies bridge steel and E identifies the −40°C Charpy V-notch quality grade. The specified minimum yield strength remains thickness-dependent.": "Q690qE 是符合 GB/T 714—2025 的 Q690 强度级桥梁用结构钢。小写 q 表示桥梁用钢，E 表示 −40°C 夏比 V 型缺口冲击韧性质量等级。规定最小屈服强度仍取决于厚度。",
  "Delivery condition: read the certificate": "交货状态：以质量证明书为准",
  "The delivery route is not encoded in the name Q690qE. GB/T 714-2025 permits thermomechanical rolling (TMCP), TMCP followed by tempering, or quenching and tempering, with the actual delivery condition stated on the quality certificate. Describing all Q690qE as “TMCP + tempered” is therefore too restrictive. Welding decisions must use the delivered product and certificate, not the grade name alone.": "Q690qE 牌号本身不包含交货工艺信息。GB/T 714—2025 允许以热机械轧制（TMCP）、TMCP 后回火或调质状态交货，实际交货状态应在质量证明书中注明。因此，把所有 Q690qE 概括为“TMCP＋回火”过于绝对。焊接决策必须依据实际交付产品及其证书，而不能只看牌号。",
  "Base-grade requirements and supplementary requirements": "基本牌号要求与附加要求",
  "The base standard controls matters including chemical composition, weldability indicators, tensile properties and impact properties. Other requirements must be identified separately in the order, drawings and project specification.": "基本标准对化学成分、焊接性指标、拉伸性能和冲击性能等作出规定。其他要求必须在订单、图纸和项目技术规格中单独明确。",
  "Requirement": "要求",
  "Correct interpretation": "准确理解",
  "Through-thickness properties": "厚度方向性能",
  "Not inherent in Q690qE. Where required, a Z15, Z25 or Z35 suffix is added and the corresponding requirements of GB/T 5313 apply.": "Q690qE 本身并不自动包含该性能。需要时，应在牌号后加 Z15、Z25 或 Z35，并满足 GB/T 5313 的相应要求。",
  "Fatigue performance": "疲劳性能",
  "Not established by the grade name. Fatigue resistance depends strongly on the structural detail, weld geometry, imperfection level, residual stress, fabrication quality and applicable design rules.": "不能通过牌号确定。疲劳抗力强烈取决于结构细节、焊缝几何、缺欠水平、残余应力、制造质量及适用设计规则。",
  "Parent-plate ultrasonic testing": "母材钢板超声检测",
  "Any required class, extent and acceptance criteria must be stated in the procurement or project documents.": "所需等级、检测范围和验收准则必须在采购或项目文件中明确。",
  "Yield ratio or tighter property limits": "屈强比或更严格的性能限值",
  "Use the requirements of the invoked edition plus any explicitly agreed supplementary limits; do not infer them from q alone.": "应采用指定标准版本的要求及明确约定的附加限值，不能只根据 q 推定。",
  "Why Q690qE is not simply “Q690E for bridges”": "为什么 Q690qE 不只是“桥梁用 Q690E”",
  "A material designation is meaningful only together with its product standard. The shorthand Q690E may refer to a product supplied under a different Chinese standard, with different chemistry, delivery conditions, thickness ranges and test requirements. Calling it “engineering-machinery steel” is not a sufficiently precise technical definition. Q690qE and a Q690E product must not be treated as interchangeable unless the governing design and material requirements have been compared and substitution has been formally accepted.": "材料牌号只有与产品标准同时使用才具有完整意义。Q690E 这一简称可能指按其他中国标准供货的产品，其化学成分、交货状态、厚度范围和试验要求可能不同。将其笼统称为“工程机械用钢”并不是足够准确的技术定义。只有在比较了适用设计与材料要求，并正式批准材料代用后，才可将 Q690qE 与某种 Q690E 产品互换使用。",
  "Comparison with S690QL": "与 S690QL 的比较",
  "S690QL is the more direct EN comparison when the purpose is to explain the impact-quality suffix: Q690qE and S690QL both specify Charpy impact properties at −40°C. S690QL1 instead specifies impact properties at −60°C.": "如果比较目的是解释冲击韧性质量后缀，S690QL 是更直接的欧标对照：Q690qE 与 S690QL 都规定了 −40°C 夏比冲击性能；S690QL1 则规定 −60°C 冲击性能。",
  "Item": "项目",
  "Product standard": "产品标准",
  "GB/T 714-2025, structural steel for bridges": "GB/T 714—2025《桥梁用结构钢》",
  "EN 10025-6:2019+A1:2022, high-yield-strength structural-steel flat products": "EN 10025-6:2019+A1:2022，高屈服强度结构钢扁平产品",
  "Strength number": "强度数字",
  "690 MPa minimum yield strength only within the specified thickness range; lower values apply above 50 mm": "只在规定厚度范围内最小屈服强度为 690 MPa；厚度大于 50 mm 时采用较低规定值",
  "690 MPa minimum yield strength at thickness up to 50 mm; EN 10025-6 gives thickness-dependent values": "厚度不大于 50 mm 时最小屈服强度为 690 MPa；EN 10025-6 规定了随厚度变化的数值",
  "Delivery symbol": "交货状态符号",
  "Not contained in the grade name; confirm the certificate": "牌号中未包含；应核对质量证明书",
  "Q means quenched and tempered": "Q 表示淬火加回火（调质）",
  "Impact-quality symbol": "冲击韧性质量符号",
  "E: specified Charpy testing at −40°C": "E：在 −40°C 进行规定的夏比冲击试验",
  "L: specified impact energy at −40°C": "L：在 −40°C 规定冲击吸收能量",
  "Bridge use": "桥梁用途",
  "Product standard specifically covers bridge structural steel": "产品标准专门适用于桥梁用结构钢",
  "Not a bridge-specific grade, but its use in a bridge is a design and specification decision; it is not excluded merely because EN 10025-6 is general": "并非桥梁专用牌号，但是否用于桥梁由设计和技术规格决定；不能仅因 EN 10025-6 是通用产品标准就排除其桥梁应用",
  "The shared number 690 does not make the grades equivalent. Strength, toughness, chemical composition, delivery condition, dimensions, inspection documentation, execution rules and design assumptions all require comparison.": "两个牌号都有 690 并不意味着它们等同。必须比较强度、韧性、化学成分、交货状态、尺寸、检验文件、施工规则和设计假定。",
  "Welding implications": "焊接方面的含义",
  "Q690qE should not be labelled simply as having “high cold-cracking sensitivity” without the actual product data and joint conditions. Hydrogen-assisted cracking risk depends on composition and delivered microstructure together with plate thickness, heat input, preheat and interpass temperature, diffusible hydrogen, joint restraint and weld-metal strength. A defensible welding review should therefore:": "在没有实际产品数据和接头条件时，不应简单将 Q690qE 标记为“冷裂纹敏感性高”。氢致裂纹风险取决于化学成分和交货组织，也取决于板厚、热输入、预热及层间温度、扩散氢、接头拘束和焊缝金属强度。因此，可追溯的焊接评审应：",
  "confirm the standard edition, full grade, dimensions, delivery condition and inspection certificate;": "确认标准版本、完整牌号、尺寸、交货状态和检验证明书；",
  "use the applicable CEV or Pcm information for the delivered product;": "使用实际交付产品适用的 CEV 或 Pcm 数据；",
  "define consumable hydrogen control, joint restraint and the thermal window;": "明确焊材氢控制、接头拘束及热循环窗口；",
  "qualify the material group, thickness, joint and welding sequence under the governing procedure standard; and": "按适用的工艺评定标准，对材料组别、厚度、接头和焊接顺序进行评定；以及",
  "verify all required tensile, impact, hardness and NDT results before transferring limits to production.": "在将工艺限值转入生产前，核实所有规定的拉伸、冲击、硬度和无损检测结果。",
  "A grade name is the starting point for material identification, not a substitute for the certificate, purchase specification, design rules or qualified welding procedure.": "牌号是材料识别的起点，不能代替质量证明书、采购技术规格、设计规则或经评定的焊接工艺。",
  "National Standard Information Service · GB/T 714-2025 Structural steel for bridge ↗": "国家标准全文公开系统 · GB/T 714—2025《桥梁用结构钢》 ↗",
  "National Standard Information Service · GB/T 5313-2023 Through-thickness properties ↗": "国家标准全文公开系统 · GB/T 5313—2023《厚度方向性能钢板》 ↗",
  "SIST preview · EN 10025-6:2019+A1:2022 ↗": "SIST 标准预览 · EN 10025-6:2019+A1:2022 ↗",
  "Q690qE: Reading the Grade Designation Correctly": "Q690qE 牌号的准确解读",
  "Material identification": "材料识别",

  "The yield ratio compares the onset of yielding with the maximum engineering stress in a tensile test. It is useful for judging strength reserve beyond yield, but it is not a stand-alone measure of ductility, toughness, seismic energy dissipation or fracture safety.": "屈强比用于比较拉伸试验中的屈服起点与最大工程应力。它有助于判断屈服后的强度储备，但不能单独评价延性、韧性、抗震耗能能力或断裂安全性。",
  "Definition and terminology": "定义与术语",
  "Yield ratio:": "屈强比：",
  "yield strength divided by tensile strength. The correct numerator depends on the material response and the governing product standard.": "屈服强度除以抗拉强度。分子应采用哪一种屈服性能，取决于材料的拉伸响应和适用产品标准。",
  "ReL is the lower yield strength, ReH is the upper yield strength, Rp0.2 is the 0.2% proof strength and Rm is the tensile strength. EN 10025-6 tabulates ReH for S690QL, while Rp0.2 is used when the tensile response does not show a distinct yield phenomenon. A reported ratio should therefore identify whether it is ReL/Rm, ReH/Rm or Rp0.2/Rm.": "ReL 为下屈服强度，ReH 为上屈服强度，Rp0.2 为 0.2% 规定塑性延伸强度，Rm 为抗拉强度。EN 10025-6 的 S690QL 表中采用 ReH；拉伸响应没有明显屈服现象时则采用 Rp0.2。因此，报告屈强比时应明确它是 ReL/Rm、ReH/Rm 还是 Rp0.2/Rm。",
  "These properties are determined by a tensile test; ISO 6892-1 defines the room-temperature test method. A measured yield ratio should use the paired yield and tensile results from the same test result. It should not be assembled by dividing unrelated values from different heats, specimens or tables.": "这些性能通过拉伸试验测定；ISO 6892-1 规定了室温拉伸试验方法。实测屈强比应采用同一试验记录中配对的屈服强度和抗拉强度结果，不能用不同炉批、试样或表格中的无关数值拼凑计算。",
  "Design standards often express the related requirement in the inverse form, fu/fy. A maximum ReL/Rm and a minimum fu/fy describe the same direction of control, but measured test values and nominal design values are not automatically interchangeable.": "设计标准常以倒数形式表达相关要求，即 fu/fy。最大 ReL/Rm 与最小 fu/fy 表示相同的控制方向，但实测试验值与名义设计值不能自动互换。",
  "What the ratio can indicate": "屈强比可以说明什么",
  "Engineering question": "工程问题",
  "What the yield ratio contributes": "屈强比提供的信息",
  "Strength reserve after first yield": "初始屈服后的强度储备",
  "A lower ratio means a larger stress interval between yield strength and tensile strength. It generally indicates more strain-hardening reserve before the maximum engineering stress is reached.": "较低的屈强比意味着屈服强度与抗拉强度之间的应力间隔较大，通常表示达到最大工程应力前具有更多的应变硬化储备。",
  "Plastic redistribution and capacity design": "塑性重分布与能力设计",
  "The separation between yield and tensile strength helps establish a hierarchy between yielding and fracture-controlled limit states. It is one input when design rules rely on plastic redistribution or component overstrength.": "屈服强度与抗拉强度之间的差距有助于建立屈服与断裂控制极限状态之间的层级关系。当设计规则依赖塑性重分布或构件超强时，屈强比是其中一项输入。",
  "Comparison of production results": "生产试验结果比较",
  "For the same product specification, thickness, delivery condition and test orientation, the ratio can help identify unusually small separation between measured yield and tensile strengths.": "在产品标准、厚度、交货状态和试验方向相同的条件下，屈强比可帮助识别实测屈服强度与抗拉强度间隔异常偏小的情况。",
  "The ratio is a stress ratio, not a strain measurement. Saying that a lower value creates a larger “plastic deformation interval” is therefore imprecise unless elongation or the full stress–strain curve is also available.": "屈强比是应力之比，不是应变测量值。因此，如果没有断后伸长率或完整应力—应变曲线，仅凭较低屈强比就断言存在更大的“塑性变形区间”并不严谨。",
  "What high and low values mean": "屈强比高低分别意味着什么",
  "In physical terms, yielding marks the start of permanent deformation. A high yield ratio means that, when permanent deformation begins, only a small increase in nominal stress remains before the tensile test reaches its maximum load. A lower ratio means that strain hardening can raise the stress by a larger amount after yielding before that maximum is reached.": "从物理意义上说，屈服标志着永久变形开始。屈强比较高时，材料一开始发生永久变形，距离拉伸试验的最大载荷就只剩较小的名义应力增量。屈强比较低时，材料屈服后可通过应变硬化继续提高应力，达到最大载荷前的强度增量更大。",
  "Relative value": "相对数值",
  "Direct interpretation": "直接含义",
  "What must not be concluded": "不能由此直接推定",
  "High ratio, closer to 1.00": "屈强比较高，接近 1.00",
  "Yield strength is close to tensile strength. The material has a smaller stress margin between first yield and maximum engineering stress, indicating less strain-hardening reserve in strength terms.": "屈服强度接近抗拉强度。从初始屈服到最大工程应力之间的应力裕量较小，表示按强度衡量的应变硬化储备较少。",
  "It does not by itself prove low elongation, brittle behaviour or poor seismic performance.": "不能仅凭这一数值证明伸长率低、材料呈脆性行为或抗震性能差。",
  "Lower ratio": "屈强比较低",
  "Yield strength is farther below tensile strength. The stress margin and indicated strain-hardening reserve are larger.": "屈服强度与抗拉强度的间隔较大，所反映的应力裕量和应变硬化储备也较大。",
  "It does not by itself prove adequate ductility, toughness or energy-dissipation capacity.": "不能仅凭这一数值证明延性、韧性或耗能能力足够。",
  "Simple example:": "简单例子：",
  "suppose two tensile specimens both have Rm = 800 MPa. If specimen A yields at 760 MPa, its ratio is 760/800 = 0.95 and the stress interval from yield to Rm is only 40 MPa. If specimen B yields at 640 MPa, its ratio is 0.80 and the interval is 160 MPa. Specimen B therefore has the larger post-yield strength reserve before maximum load.": "假设两个拉伸试样的 Rm 均为 800 MPa。试样 A 在 760 MPa 屈服，屈强比为 760/800 = 0.95，从屈服到 Rm 的应力间隔只有 40 MPa。试样 B 在 640 MPa 屈服，屈强比为 0.80，应力间隔为 160 MPa。因此，试样 B 在达到最大载荷前具有更大的屈服后强度储备。",
  "This is the physical meaning of the ratio: it describes the nominal stress reserve after yielding, not how close the steel is to fracture. Rm is the maximum engineering stress, not the fracture stress; deformation can continue after Rm as necking develops. Elongation, toughness and fracture behaviour must still be assessed separately.": "这就是屈强比的物理意义：它描述屈服后还剩多少名义应力储备，而不是材料“离断裂还有多近”。Rm 是最大工程应力，不是断裂应力；发生颈缩后，材料仍可继续变形。仍需分别评估伸长率、韧性和断裂行为。",
  "Is there a preferred range?": "是否存在理想范围",
  "There is no universal optimum range for all steels and structures. The acceptable value depends on the product standard, steel grade, thickness, structural design method, applicable National Annex and any project-specific capacity-design or procurement requirements.": "不存在适用于所有钢材和结构的通用最优范围。可接受数值取决于产品标准、钢级、厚度、结构设计方法、适用国家附录，以及项目特定的能力设计或采购要求。",
  "Eurocode limits are acceptance boundaries, not target bands. Under EN 1993-1-1:2022, the recommended fu/fy limits correspond to fy/fu ceilings of about 0.91 for plastic global analysis and about 0.95 for elastic global analysis, unless the National Annex gives different values. These limits do not mean that 0.91 or 0.95 is an ideal value; they state the minimum separation required by the relevant design assumption.": "欧标限值是验收边界，不是目标区间。按照 EN 1993-1-1:2022，在国家附录未另行规定时，推荐的 fu/fy 限值分别对应：塑性整体分析时 fy/fu 上限约为 0.91，弹性整体分析时约为 0.95。这并不表示 0.91 或 0.95 是理想值，而是说明相应设计假定所要求的最小强度间隔。",
  "How the parameter is used": "工程上如何使用这一参数",
  "Define the ratio correctly.": "正确定义屈强比。",
  "State whether the numerator is ReL, ReH, Rp0.2 or nominal fy, and use the corresponding Rm or nominal fu from the same basis.": "明确分子采用 ReL、ReH、Rp0.2 还是名义 fy，并采用同一依据下相应的 Rm 或名义 fu。",
  "Apply the governing limit.": "采用适用限值。",
  "Check the product standard, design standard, National Annex and project specification. Do not invent a general acceptance range.": "核对产品标准、设计标准、国家附录和项目技术规格，不能自行设定通用验收范围。",
  "Keep nominal and measured values separate.": "区分名义值与实测值。",
  "Nominal fy/fu is used where the design rule requires product-standard values; an actual test ratio uses paired results from one tensile test.": "设计规则要求采用产品标准数值时使用名义 fy/fu；实测屈强比则采用同一次拉伸试验中的配对结果。",
  "Check companion properties.": "同时核查相关性能。",
  "Review elongation, toughness, fracture requirements, cyclic behaviour and connection detailing separately whenever they are relevant.": "在相关情况下，分别核查伸长率、韧性、断裂性能要求、循环性能和连接构造。",
  "What the ratio cannot establish by itself": "屈强比不能单独证明什么",
  "Property": "性能",
  "Evidence needed in addition to yield ratio": "除屈强比外还需哪些证据",
  "Ductility": "延性",
  "Elongation after fracture, uniform elongation or strain at maximum force, and—where relevant—the complete stress–strain response.": "断后伸长率、均匀延伸率或最大力总延伸率，以及适用时的完整应力—应变响应。",
  "Resistance to brittle fracture": "抗脆性断裂能力",
  "Applicable Charpy impact requirements, fracture-toughness data where specified, service temperature, thickness, stress state and flaw assumptions.": "适用的夏比冲击要求、规定时的断裂韧度数据、服役温度、厚度、应力状态和缺陷假定。",
  "Seismic or cyclic energy dissipation": "抗震或循环耗能能力",
  "Cyclic material and component behaviour, local-buckling resistance, connection detailing, weld and heat-affected-zone properties, loading history and system-level design rules.": "材料和构件的循环性能、局部屈曲抗力、连接构造、焊缝及热影响区性能、加载历程和体系层面的设计规则。",
  "Fatigue resistance": "疲劳抗力",
  "Detail category, weld geometry, imperfections, residual stress, stress range and inspection or execution quality.": "细节类别、焊缝几何、缺欠、残余应力、应力范围以及检验或施工质量。",
  "A high yield ratio does not prove that a steel will fail suddenly after first yield. Conversely, a low ratio does not prove adequate toughness or cyclic ductility. The Hong Kong Code of Practice for the Structural Use of Steel treats strength, resistance to brittle fracture, ductility and weldability as separate essential material requirements; that separation is a useful engineering discipline.": "高屈强比不能证明钢材会在初始屈服后突然断裂；反过来，低屈强比也不能证明材料具有足够的韧性或循环延性。香港《钢结构使用守则》把强度、抗脆性断裂能力、延性和焊接性列为彼此独立的基本材料要求；这种区分是一项重要的工程原则。",
  "Eurocode interpretation": "欧标设计语境下的理解",
  "EN 1993-1-1:2022 addresses material ductility through more than one criterion. Unless the relevant National Annex gives different values, its recommended limits include fu/fy ≥ 1.10 with elongation at failure ≥ 15% for plastic global analysis, and fu/fy ≥ 1.05 with elongation at failure ≥ 12% for elastic global analysis. The corresponding yield-ratio ceilings are approximately 0.91 and 0.95 respectively.": "EN 1993-1-1:2022 通过多项指标控制材料延性。除非相关国家附录另有规定，其推荐限值包括：采用塑性整体分析时 fu/fy ≥ 1.10 且断后伸长率不小于 15%；采用弹性整体分析时 fu/fy ≥ 1.05 且断后伸长率不小于 12%。相应的屈强比上限分别约为 0.91 和 0.95。",
  "This is the important point: even Eurocode 3 does not use a strength ratio alone as a complete statement of ductility. The applicable product standard, design method and National Annex must all be identified.": "关键在于：即使 Eurocode 3 也不会仅凭一个强度比完整评价延性。必须同时明确适用产品标准、设计方法和国家附录。",
  "S690QL worked example": "S690QL 示例",
  "S690QL is a quenched-and-tempered high-yield-strength structural steel for flat products under EN 10025-6:2019+A1:2022. For nominal thickness from 3 mm up to and including 50 mm, the product standard specifies a minimum yield strength ReH of 690 MPa, a tensile-strength range Rm of 770–940 MPa and a minimum elongation after fracture A of 14%. The L quality designates the specified Charpy impact properties at −40°C.": "S690QL 是 EN 10025-6:2019+A1:2022 规定的调质高屈服强度结构钢扁平产品。公称厚度为 3 mm 至 50 mm（含）时，产品标准规定最小屈服强度 ReH 为 690 MPa、抗拉强度 Rm 为 770～940 MPa、最小断后伸长率 A 为 14%。质量等级 L 表示规定了 −40°C 夏比冲击性能。",
  "EN 10025-6 property": "EN 10025-6 性能项目",
  "S690QL, 3 mm ≤ t ≤ 50 mm": "S690QL，3 mm ≤ t ≤ 50 mm",
  "Delivery condition": "交货状态",
  "Quenched and tempered": "淬火加回火（调质）",
  "Minimum yield strength ReH": "最小屈服强度 ReH",
  "690 MPa": "690 MPa",
  "Tensile strength Rm": "抗拉强度 Rm",
  "770–940 MPa": "770～940 MPa",
  "Minimum elongation after fracture A": "最小断后伸长率 A",
  "14%": "14%",
  "Impact-quality designation": "冲击韧性质量等级",
  "QL: specified Charpy properties at −40°C": "QL：规定 −40°C 夏比冲击性能",
  "Nominal comparison is not a measured yield ratio": "名义值比较不等于实测屈强比",
  "Using the specified minimum strengths for the thickness band above gives 690/770 = 0.896, or inversely 770/690 = 1.116. This is a comparison of nominal product-standard values and is relevant where a design rule calls for nominal fy and fu. It is not the measured ReH/Rm ratio of a delivered plate and it is not an acceptance ceiling of 0.896 for every tensile test.": "采用上述厚度范围的规定最小强度，可得 690/770 = 0.896；倒数为 770/690 = 1.116。这是产品标准名义值之间的比较，适用于设计规则要求采用名义 fy 和 fu 的情形。它既不是交付钢板的实测 ReH/Rm，也不是每次拉伸试验均须满足的 0.896 验收上限。",
  "An actual S690QL result must be calculated from the paired yield and tensile strengths reported for the same tensile test. The actual yield strength may exceed 690 MPa and the actual tensile strength may lie anywhere within the permitted range. For plate thicker than 50 mm, EN 10025-6 uses different strength bands, so the 690/770 comparison must not be reused.": "S690QL 的实测屈强比必须采用同一次拉伸试验报告中配对的屈服强度和抗拉强度计算。实际屈服强度可以高于 690 MPa，实际抗拉强度也可处于允许范围内的不同位置。板厚大于 50 mm 时，EN 10025-6 采用不同的强度分档，因此不能继续套用 690/770。",
  "Correct statement:": "准确表述：",
  "for S690QL plate up to 50 mm, 0.896 is the ratio of the specified minimum ReH to the specified minimum Rm. The measured material yield ratio must come from paired certificate or test results.": "对于厚度不大于 50 mm 的 S690QL 钢板，0.896 是规定最小 ReH 与规定最小 Rm 之比；材料实测屈强比必须由质量证明书或试验记录中的配对结果计算。",
  "Why a grade does not have one fixed measured ratio": "为什么一个牌号没有唯一固定的实测屈强比",
  "S690QL identifies a product-standard grade, delivery condition and impact-quality level; it does not define one stress–strain curve for every heat and thickness. Statements such as “S690 has a yield ratio of 0.90” or “S355 has a yield ratio of 0.65” may describe selected nominal values or a particular test result, but neither is a universal measured property of the grade.": "S690QL 表示产品标准牌号、交货状态和冲击韧性质量等级，但不会为每个炉批和每种厚度规定同一条应力—应变曲线。“S690 的屈强比为 0.90”或“S355 的屈强比为 0.65”等说法，可能描述所选名义值或某次具体试验结果，但都不是该牌号通用且固定的实测性能。",
  "The distinction matters for high-strength steel. EN 1993-1-1 requires the applicable ductility checks to be satisfied, while the project design route and National Annex determine how S690 is used. Product-standard compliance, nominal design properties and actual certificate results should be recorded as three different things.": "这一区分对高强钢尤其重要。EN 1993-1-1 要求满足适用的延性验算，而项目设计路径和国家附录决定 S690 的具体使用方式。产品标准符合性、名义设计性能和质量证明书实测结果应作为三类不同信息分别记录。",
  "Strength utilisation and economy": "强度利用与经济性",
  "A lower yield ratio does not mean that tensile strength is simply “wasted”. Many structural checks are governed by yield, stability, serviceability or fatigue rather than tensile rupture, so a large gap between yield and tensile strength may not translate directly into weight savings. Equally, the highest possible ratio is not an economic target because some design assumptions require reserve beyond yield.": "较低的屈强比并不意味着抗拉强度被简单“浪费”。许多结构验算由屈服、稳定、正常使用或疲劳控制，而不是由拉断控制，因此屈服强度与抗拉强度之间较大的差距未必直接转化为减重收益。同样，屈强比也不是越高越经济，因为某些设计假定要求屈服后仍有强度储备。",
  "The correct objective is compliance with the material product standard, structural design rules and project specification—not an isolated attempt to maximise or minimise the ratio.": "正确目标是满足材料产品标准、结构设计规则和项目技术规格，而不是孤立地追求屈强比最大或最小。",
  "Practical review checklist": "工程审核清单",
  "Identify whether the reported quantity is ReL/Rm, ReH/Rm, Rp0.2/Rm or nominal fy/fu.": "确认所报告的量是 ReL/Rm、ReH/Rm、Rp0.2/Rm，还是名义 fy/fu。",
  "Confirm the product standard and edition, grade, product form, thickness, delivery condition and test orientation.": "确认产品标准及版本、牌号、产品形式、厚度、交货状态和试验方向。",
  "For an actual material ratio, use paired results from the same tensile test record.": "计算材料实测屈强比时，应使用同一拉伸试验记录中的配对结果。",
  "Locate the requirement in the product standard, design standard, National Annex, purchase specification or contract; state which document controls.": "在产品标准、设计标准、国家附录、采购技术规格或合同中查明要求，并明确哪份文件具有控制作用。",
  "Review elongation, toughness, weldability and any cyclic or fracture requirements separately.": "分别审核伸长率、韧性、焊接性以及任何循环或断裂性能要求。",
  "Where AWS D1.1 or another welding code applies, use it for the welding controls within its scope; do not treat it as a substitute for the material product specification or structural design criteria.": "当适用 AWS D1.1 或其他焊接规范时，应在其范围内用于焊接控制；不能把它当作材料产品标准或结构设计准则的替代文件。",
  "Technical conclusion:": "技术结论：",
  "use the yield ratio to quantify the separation between yield strength and tensile strength. A high value means a smaller strength reserve beyond yield; a lower value means a larger reserve. Acceptance must come from the governing standard and design method, and the ratio must not replace separate checks of elongation, toughness, fracture resistance or cyclic performance.": "屈强比用于量化屈服强度与抗拉强度之间的间隔。数值较高表示屈服后的强度储备较小，数值较低表示储备较大。是否合格必须依据适用标准和设计方法确定；屈强比不能代替对伸长率、韧性、抗断裂能力或循环性能的单独核查。",
  "UNI · EN 10025-6:2019+A1:2022 High-yield-strength structural-steel flat products ↗": "UNI · EN 10025-6:2019+A1:2022《高屈服强度结构钢扁平产品技术交货条件》 ↗",
  "ArcelorMittal Industeel · S690QL Declaration of Performance ↗": "ArcelorMittal Industeel · S690QL 性能声明 ↗",
  "ISO · ISO 6892-1:2019 Metallic materials—Tensile testing at room temperature ↗": "ISO · ISO 6892-1:2019《金属材料 拉伸试验 第 1 部分：室温试验方法》 ↗",
  "UNI · EN 1993-1-1:2022 Eurocode 3—General rules and rules for buildings ↗": "UNI · EN 1993-1-1:2022《欧洲规范 3：钢结构设计——通用规则和建筑物规则》 ↗",
  "Hong Kong Buildings Department · Code of Practice for the Structural Use of Steel 2011 (2023 Edition) ↗": "香港屋宇署 ·《钢结构使用守则 2011》（2023 年版）↗",
  "American Welding Society · AWS D1.1/D1.1M:2025 Structural Welding Code—Steel ↗": "美国焊接学会 · AWS D1.1/D1.1M:2025《钢结构焊接规范》 ↗",
  "Yield-to-Tensile Strength Ratio in Structural Steel": "结构钢屈强比：以 S690QL 为例",
  "Mechanical properties": "力学性能"
};
